, and use `files.read` for a known range or to expand relevant results. Full file size: 1663 file lines.\n[L1] ================================================================================\n[L2] HANDOFF A\n[L3] GCE STACK — GOOGLE DRIVE CABLE CAR / PIGEON TRANSPORT ARCHITECTURE\n[L4] ================================================================================\n\n[L6] DATE: 2026-09-24\n[L7] AUTHORITY: Don\n[L8] SEAT: Coda — Strategic Advisor / Governance\n[L9] PROJECT: GCE Stack Projects\n[L10] WORKSTREAM: DevPad / myDon / Cable Car / Pigeon\n[L11] STATUS: DESIGN LANE READY FOR RECON + SPECIFICATION\n[L12] IMPLEMENTATION: NOT STARTED\n[L13] CONFIDENCE: 98%\n\n[L15] ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n[L16] 1. PURPOSE\n[L17] ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n[L19] This handoff preserves the current design state for creating a fast, reliable,\n[L20] two-way transport path between Coda/Don and the local GCE Command Center.\n\n[L22] The problem being solved is not browser embedding.\n\n[L24] The real problem is:\n\n[L26] DON SHOULD NOT BE THE CLIPBOARD BUS.\n\n[L28] Current manual friction:\n\n[L30] Coda creates prompt/handoff\n[L31] → Don copies it\n[L32] → Don finds correct terminal\n[L33] → Don pastes it\n[L34] → target model runs\n[L35] → target returns result\n[L36] → Don copies result back\n[L37] → Coda reconciles\n[L38] → repeat\n\n[L40] This becomes increasingly expensive as:\n\n[L42] - projects multiply;\n[L43] - seats remain persistent;\n[L44] - models/runtime providers change;\n[L45] - credits expire;\n[L46] - terminals fail;\n[L47] - Don works from laptop/TV/phone;\n[L48] - multiple workstreams run concurrently.\n\n[L50] The desired operating state is:\n\n[L52] Don talks to Coda\n[L53] → Coda creates structured handoff\n[L54] → transport layer carries it\n[L55] → local GCE inbox receives it\n[L56] → myDon presents/routes it\n[L57] → target seat acts\n[L58] → result returns through same transport\n[L59] → Coda/Don continue without manual copy/paste.\n\n[L61] ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n[L62] 2. CURRENT VERIFIED LOCAL ARCHITECTURE\n[L63] ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n[L65] Main DevPad / Command Center:\n\n[L67] C:\\Users\\Dekan AI Brother\\GCE_DON\\command-center\\\n\n[L69] Current main board:\n\n[L71] Coda      | Chiave      | Vittorio\n[L72] Nico      | VoiceBridge | Luce\n[L73] Talon     | Keel        | Falcon\n\n[L75] Core doctrine:\n\n[L77] IDENTITY != ROLE != MODEL != RUNTIME != PROVIDER\n[L78] MODEL != SEAT\n[L79] TILE != SEAT != MODEL != RUNTIME != PROVIDER\n\n[L81] The Main DevPad is the stable project/work surface.\n\n[L83] A second DevPad is now conceptually scoped:\n\n[L85] ROOKIE DEVPAD\n\n[L87] Purpose:\n\n[L89] - ad hoc work;\n[L90] - experiments;\n[L91] - scratch sessions;\n[L92] - temporary model auditions;\n[L93] - overflow;\n[L94] - quick one-off jobs;\n[L95] - backup capacity.\n\n[L97] The orchestration layer is:\n\n[L99] myDon / Don Controller\n\n[L101] Main DevPad = project cockpit\n[L102] Rookie DevPad = ad hoc cockpit\n[L103] myDon = orchestration/controller surface\n\n[L105] ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n[L106] 3. CURRENT INBOX GROUND TRUTH\n[L107] ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n[L109] Luce completed read-only inbox recon.\n\n[L111] Grounded conclusion:\n\n[L113] THE EXISTING INBOX ALREADY IS THE QUEUE.\n\n[L115] Canonical unrouted pool:\n\n[L117] _shared\\\n\n[L119] Route model:\n\n[L121] _shared\\<handoff-id>.json\n[L122]         ↓ Don selects target\n[L123] <target-seat>\\<same-handoff-id>.json\n[L124]         ↓ target consumes\n[L125] _archive\\\n\n[L127] Branch:\n\n[L129] BRANCH A — EXISTING INBOX IS CANONICAL QUEUE\n[L130] VARIANT: WRITE-ROUTE / MOVE-WITH-ID\n\n[L132] Important ground truth:\n\n[L134] 1. Canonical handoff identity is the filename.\n\n[L136] 2. Internal JSON \"id\" cannot be treated as canonical because live files exist\n[L137]    where filename and internal id differ.\n\n[L139] 3. Routing is not assign-in-place through inbox MCP.\n\n[L141] 4. Routing is a controlled file move preserving the canonical filename.\n\n[L143] 5. Routable targets must come from the SEAT REGISTRY.\n\n[L145] 6. Filesystem directory names are not routing authority.\n\n[L147] 7. inbox-mcp should remain frozen for V1 rather than being redesigned.\n\n[L149] 8. myDon requires only minimal routing/audit residue.\n\n[L151] ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n[L152] 4. CURRENT myDon DIRECTION\n[L153] ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n[L155] Recommended surfaces:\n\n[L157] http://localhost:4727/\n[L158] → Main DevPad\n\n[L160] http://localhost:4727/mydon\n[L161] → Don orchestration/controller surface\n\nSame:\n\n[L165] - Node server;\n[L166] - registry;\n[L167] - control plane;\n[L168] - inbox;\n[L169] - WebSocket infrastructure where appropriate.\n\n[L171] Different UX purpose.\n\n[L173] myDon Phase 1:\n\n[L175] _shared item visible\n[L176] → Don selects seat\n[L177] → controlled move to seat inbox\n[L178] → delivery verified\n[L179] → status shown ROUTED\n[L180] → next pending item selected.\n\n[L182] No new queue database.\n\n[L184] No event-sourcing architecture unless later evidence requires it.\n\n[L186] No second seat registry.\n\n[L188] No autonomous agent-to-agent routing.\n\n[L190] Don remains authority.\n\n[L192] ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n[L193] 5. CABLE CAR / PIGEON DISTINCTION\n[L194] ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n[L196] These concepts must remain separate.\n\n[L198] CABLE CAR\n\n[L200] The transport path / bridge.\n\n[L202] It answers:\n\n[L204] HOW does information move between the external Coda surface and the local GCE\n[L205] estate?\n\n[L207] Potential technologies:\n\n[L209] - Google Drive;\n[L210] - dedicated email;\n[L211] - Proton Bridge IMAP/SMTP;\n[L212] - local sync;\n[L213] - future API transport;\n[L214] - hybrid mechanisms.\n\n[L216] PIGEON\n\n[L218] The courier behavior / transport seat.\n\n[L220] It answers:\n\n[L222] WHO performs bounded delivery/confirmation behavior?\n\n[L224] Pigeon responsibilities:\n\n[L226] - receive an already-addressed envelope;\n[L227] - validate required metadata;\n[L228] - transport it;\n[L229] - confirm delivery;\n[L230] - correlate a return;\n[L231] - preserve handoff identity;\n[L232] - report failure clearly.\n\n[L234] Pigeon must NOT:\n\n[L236] - infer substantive routing authority;\n[L237] - reinterpret the handoff;\n[L238] - choose architecture;\n[L239] - rewrite instructions;\n[L240] - select a seat based on model/runtime;\n[L241] - silently reroute failures.\n\n[L243] Core principle:\n\n[L245] CABLE CAR = PATH\n[L246] PIGEON = COURIER\n\nAnd:\n\n[L250] TRANSPORT != INTERPRETER\n[L251] TRANSPORT != AUTHORITY\n\n[L253] ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n[L254] 6. WHY GOOGLE DRIVE IS NOW A SERIOUS CANDIDATE\n[L255] ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n[L257] Google Drive initially looked potentially too heavy for high-frequency routing.\n\n[L259] That concern remains valid if Drive itself becomes the queue.\n\n[L261] However, a cleaner model has emerged:\n\n[L263] GOOGLE DRIVE IS NOT THE LIVE QUEUE.\n\n[L265] The local inbox already owns that responsibility.\n\n[L267] Instead, Drive can become:\n\n[L269] - neutral external exchange surface;\n[L270] - durable handoff artifact store;\n[L271] - Coda/Don accessible bridge;\n[L272] - cross-device access point;\n[L273] - storage for long-form artifacts;\n[L274] - payload staging area;\n[L275] - return-artifact location.\n\n[L277] This removes one major conceptual problem.\n\n[L279] Drive does not need to replace:\n\n[L281] _shared\n[L282] seat inboxes\n[L283] myDon queue projection\n\n[L285] Drive can simply bridge external Coda work into the local estate.\n\n[L287] ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n[L288] 7. PROPOSED GOOGLE DRIVE CABLE CAR SHAPE\n[L289] ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n[L291] Conceptual flow:\n\n[L293] CODA / DON\n    ↓\n[L295] Google Drive handoff artifact\n    ↓\n[L297] Pigeon / local watcher / MCP adapter\n    ↓\n[L299] local GCE inbox _shared\n    ↓\nmyDon\n    ↓\n[L303] Don selects target\n    ↓\n[L305] seat inbox\n    ↓\n[L307] target performs work\n    ↓\n[L309] return handoff/result\n    ↓\n[L311] Pigeon\n    ↓\n[L313] Google Drive return lane\n    ↓\n[L315] CODA / DON\n\n[L317] Important:\n\n[L319] Drive is not seat authority.\n[L320] Drive is not queue authority.\n[L321] Drive is not orchestration authority.\n\n[L323] It is a transport/staging medium.\n\n[L325] ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n[L326] 8. GOOGLE DRIVE STRUCTURE — DESIGN TARGET\n[L327] ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n[L329] A dedicated isolated transport root should be evaluated rather than scattering\n[L330] handoffs through existing GCE Drive content.\n\n[L332] Working concept:\n\n[L334] GCE_CABLE_CAR/\n[L335]     00_INBOUND_TO_GCE/\n[L336]     01_OUTBOUND_FROM_GCE/\n[L337]     02_IN_FLIGHT/\n[L338]     03_ACKNOWLEDGED/\n[L339]     04_COMPLETED/\n[L340]     90_FAILED/\n[L341]     99_ARCHIVE/\n\n[L343] Alternative names are open.\n\n[L345] The important requirement is isolation.\n\n[L347] The transport lane should not pollute:\n\n[L349] - framework authority folders;\n[L350] - project canonical folders;\n[L351] - random Drive root;\n[L352] - current architectural documents.\n\n[L354] This is an operational exchange lane.\n\n[L356] ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n[L357] 9. HANDOFF ENVELOPE\n[L358] ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n[L360] Every transported handoff should use a structured envelope.\n\n[L362] Working schema:\n\n[L364] HANDOFF_ID:\n[L365] FROM_SEAT:\n[L366] TO_SEAT:\n[L367] PROJECT:\n[L368] WORKSTREAM:\nTYPE:\n[L370] PRIORITY:\n[L371] STATUS:\n[L372] CREATED_AT:\n[L373] RETURN_TO:\n\n[L375] OBJECTIVE:\n...\n\n[L378] CONTEXT:\n...\n\n[L381] INSTRUCTIONS:\n...\n\n[L384] ARTIFACTS:\n...\n\n[L387] STOP_CONDITIONS:\n...\n\n[L390] EXPECTED_RETURN:\n...\n\n[L393] Example:\n\n[L395] HANDOFF_ID: HDO-20260924-0017\n[L396] FROM_SEAT: Coda\n[L397] TO_SEAT: Luce\n[L398] PROJECT: GCE_DevPad_Command_Center\n[L399] WORKSTREAM: myDon Phase 1\n[L400] TYPE: VERIFICATION\n[L401] PRIORITY: NORMAL\n[L402] STATUS: READY_TO_TRANSPORT\n\n[L404] OBJECTIVE:\n[L405] Verify route idempotency and restart persistence.\n\n[L407] CONTEXT:\n...\n\n[L410] RETURN_TO:\n[L411] Coda / Don\n\n[L413] The filename should preserve the canonical handoff ID.\n\n[L415] Example:\n\n[L417] HDO-20260924-0017_luce_mydon_phase1.md\n\n[L419] or structured JSON where appropriate.\n\n[L421] ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n[L422] 10. TWO-WAY REQUIREMENT\n[L423] ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n[L425] The Cable Car cannot be outbound-only.\n\n[L427] Coda sends work into GCE.\n\n[L429] GCE must return:\n\n[L431] - findings;\n[L432] - implementation results;\n[L433] - verification;\n[L434] - blockers;\n[L435] - status;\n[L436] - artifacts;\n[L437] - escalation requests.\n\n[L439] The same HANDOFF_ID should survive the full round trip.\n\n[L441] Example:\n\n[L443] HDO-20260924-0017\n[L444]     outbound Coda → Luce\n[L445]     return Luce → Coda\n\n[L447] Do not mint a disconnected identity for each leg unless there is a proven need.\n\n[L449] Parent/child IDs may later be added for branching work.\n\n[L451] ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n[L452] 11. GOOGLE DRIVE MCP ROLE\n[L453] ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n[L455] The Drive integration should be evaluated for bounded operations such as:\n\n[L457] - create handoff artifact;\n[L458] - read handoff artifact;\n[L459] - move to a status folder;\n[L460] - archive completed work;\n[L461] - create return artifact;\n[L462] - inspect transport folder;\n[L463] - reconcile failed/incomplete delivery.\n\n[L465] The design should avoid requiring Don to manually:\n\n[L467] - create files;\n[L468] - rename files;\n[L469] - move files;\n[L470] - copy payloads between folders;\n[L471] - clean up routine transport residue.\n\n[L473] Automation should do routine transport housekeeping.\n\n[L475] Don should intervene only for:\n\n[L477] - routing authority;\n[L478] - conflict;\n[L479] - ambiguity;\n[L480] - escalation;\n[L481] - destructive cleanup if governance requires approval.\n\n[L483] ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n[L484] 12. DRIVE CLEANUP / ARCHIVE POLICY\n[L485] ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n[L487] Don explicitly raised concern about Drive clutter.\n\n[L489] Therefore cleanup cannot be an afterthought.\n\n[L491] Potential lifecycle:\n\nREADY\n[L494] → TRANSPORTED\n[L495] → ACKNOWLEDGED\n[L496] → COMPLETED\n[L497] → ARCHIVED\n\n[L499] Transport artifacts should not remain forever in working folders.\n\n[L501] Candidate policy:\n\n[L503] - active/in-flight handoffs remain hot;\n[L504] - completed items move automatically to archive;\n[L505] - older operational transport residue can be compacted;\n[L506] - only artifacts with durable value get promoted into project/framework areas;\n[L507] - Raven/Magpie may later help classify durable records;\n[L508] - cleanup automation should never erase canonical project records.\n\n[L510] Transport archive != project canon.\n\n[L512] ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n[L513] 13. RELATIONSHIP TO MAIN / ROOKIE DEVPAD\n[L514] ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n[L516] Cable Car should eventually be able to target either operating surface.\n\n[L518] Main DevPad:\n\n[L520] - project-bound;\n[L521] - stable seats;\n[L522] - durable active work.\n\n[L524] Rookie DevPad:\n\n[L526] - ad hoc;\n[L527] - experimental;\n[L528] - temporary runtime work.\n\n[L530] The transport envelope should identify project/workstream and desired seat, but\n[L531] must not hard-code a DevPad surface unless required.\n\n[L533] myDon may resolve the target surface based on current operating context.\n\n[L535] No permanent assumption yet that:\n\n[L537] one seat = one pad\n[L538] one physical tile = one routing endpoint\n\n[L540] ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n[L541] 14. RELATIONSHIP TO BEDROCK / OPENAI / KIMI / OTHER PROVIDERS\n[L542] ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n[L544] Compute providers remain separate.\n\n[L546] Potential Coda/runtime sources include:\n\n[L548] - ChatGPT;\n[L549] - OpenAI terminal/API if available;\n[L550] - Amazon Bedrock;\n[L551] - Kimi;\n[L552] - GLM;\n[L553] - other approved providers.\n\nBut:\n\n[L557] BEDROCK != TRANSPORT\n[L558] OPENAI != TRANSPORT\n[L559] KIMI != TRANSPORT\n[L560] OPENROUTER != TRANSPORT\n[L561] OPENCODE != TRANSPORT\n\n[L563] Cable Car should remain model/provider-neutral.\n\n[L565] The same handoff should be transportable regardless of which runtime occupies a\nseat.\n\n[L568] ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n[L569] 15. FAILURE SEMANTICS\n[L570] ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n[L572] No silent failure.\n\n[L574] Candidate hard failures:\n\n[L576] - Drive artifact missing;\n[L577] - duplicate canonical ID with conflicting payload;\n[L578] - malformed envelope;\n[L579] - unknown target seat;\n[L580] - local _shared write failure;\n[L581] - destination already exists with conflict;\n[L582] - return correlation failure;\n[L583] - archive move failure;\n[L584] - transport watcher unavailable.\n\n[L586] Required behavior:\n\n[L588] FAIL VISIBLE\n[L589] DO NOT SILENTLY REROUTE\n[L590] DO NOT OVERWRITE CONFLICTING HANDOFF\n[L591] DO NOT INVENT TARGET\n[L592] DO NOT FALL BACK TO ANOTHER MODEL/SEAT\n\n[L594] Same-ID/same-payload duplicate may be treated as idempotent success after proof.\n\n[L596] ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n[L597] 16. RECOMMENDED FIRST PROVING TEST\n[L598] ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n[L600] Do not build a giant transport system first.\n\n[L602] Prove one complete round trip.\n\nTEST:\n\n[L606] 1. Coda creates one structured handoff in isolated Drive transport folder.\n\n[L608] 2. Pigeon/local adapter detects or receives it.\n\n[L610] 3. Same canonical ID appears exactly once in local _shared.\n\n[L612] 4. myDon shows it.\n\n[L614] 5. Don routes it to Luce.\n\n[L616] 6. Luce completes work.\n\n[L618] 7. Return artifact with same HANDOFF_ID is placed in outbound transport lane.\n\n[L620] 8. Coda can read the returned result.\n\n[L622] 9. Completed transport artifacts move out of active folders.\n\n[L624] 10. Restart local Command Center and verify no duplication/replay.\n\n[L626] PASS CONDITION:\n\n[L628] One handoff can go Coda → local GCE → target seat → Coda without Don manually\n[L629] copying text.\n\n[L631] That is the milestone.\n\n[L633] ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n[L634] 17. OPEN DESIGN QUESTIONS\n[L635] ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n[L637] Do not assume answers yet.\n\n[L639] Need recon on:\n\n[L641] - exact Google Drive MCP capabilities available to this workflow;\n[L642] - write latency;\n[L643] - change detection / polling model;\n[L644] - conflict behavior;\n[L645] - move/rename semantics;\n[L646] - offline behavior;\n[L647] - local sync implications;\n[L648] - file locking;\n[L649] - canonical format: Markdown vs JSON + Markdown payload;\n[L650] - Drive permissions;\n[L651] - whether a dedicated Drive subtree or separate Drive account is useful;\n[L652] - whether local adapter should poll Drive or consume explicit actions;\n[L653] - whether Proton/email should remain a fallback lane;\n[L654] - whether Drive transport artifacts should also be mirrored locally.\n\n[L656] ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n[L657] 18. DESIGN INVARIANTS\n[L658] ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n[L660] Preserve:\n\n[L662] IDENTITY != ROLE != MODEL != RUNTIME != PROVIDER\n[L663] MODEL != SEAT\n[L664] TRANSPORT != INTERPRETER\n[L665] TRANSPORT != AUTHORITY\n[L666] PIGEON != ROUTER\n[L667] DRIVE != QUEUE AUTHORITY\n[L668] DRIVE != SEAT AUTHORITY\n[L669] RUNTIME != SEAT\n[L670] FILENAME/HANDOFF ID MUST SURVIVE TRANSPORT\n[L671] DON REMAINS ROUTING AUTHORITY\n\nAnd:\n\n[L675] One owner per responsibility.\n\n[L677] ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n[L678] 19. NEXT ROUTE\n[L679] ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n[L681] Recommended next sequence:\n\n[L683] 1. Read-only recon of current Google Drive estate relevant to transport.\n[L684] 2. Identify loose/random GCE artifacts currently living outside intended folders.\n[L685] 3. Do NOT clean them during recon unless Don explicitly approves.\n[L686] 4. Define dedicated Cable Car root/folder structure.\n[L687] 5. Verify Google Drive MCP read/write/move capabilities.\n[L688] 6. Define ex