horitative yet.\n\n[L1261] ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n[L1262] 16. PYTHON ROLE\n[L1263] ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n[L1265] Python is a strong candidate for proving adapters because it supports:\n\n[L1267] - MIDI;\n[L1268] - OSC;\n[L1269] - Bluetooth libraries;\n[L1270] - serial devices;\n[L1271] - camera CV;\n[L1272] - MediaPipe;\n[L1273] - Windows APIs;\n[L1274] - rapid experimentation.\n\nBut:\n\n[L1278] PYTHON IS NOT YET A BINDING ARCHITECTURAL REQUIREMENT.\n\n[L1280] The stable abstraction is the control-event contract.\n\n[L1282] Adapters may later be implemented in:\n\n[L1284] - Python;\n[L1285] - Node;\n[L1286] - Rust;\n[L1287] - device SDK;\n[L1288] - service daemon.\n\n[L1290] Do not architect around language choice prematurely.\n\n[L1292] ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n[L1293] 17. RELATIONSHIP TO VOICEBRIDGE\n[L1294] ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n[L1296] VoiceBridge is one input/output lane.\n\n[L1298] It must not become a second orchestration architecture.\n\n[L1300] Desired model:\n\n[L1302] VoiceBridge\nMixer\n[L1304] Gesture\n[L1305] Keyboard\nTouch\n        ↓\n[L1308] same orchestration API\n\n[L1310] VoiceBridge may also provide state events such as:\n\n[L1312] VOICE_ACTIVE\n[L1313] VOICE_IDLE\n\n[L1315] Those events may trigger audio ducking.\n\n[L1317] But VoiceBridge does not own:\n\n[L1319] - global routing;\n[L1320] - seat authority;\n[L1321] - model selection;\n[L1322] - transport authority.\n\n[L1324] ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n[L1325] 18. RELATIONSHIP TO MAIN / ROOKIE DEVPAD\n[L1326] ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n[L1328] Physical controls should eventually be able to operate either surface.\n\n[L1330] Possible examples:\n\n[L1332] CUE 