RAM cost;\n[L1405] - GPU cost;\n[L1406] - latency;\n[L1407] - background process count;\n[L1408] - reliability;\n[L1409] - thermal impact.\n\n[L1411] This matters because Main + Rookie DevPad + VoiceBridge + coding agents may already\n[L1412] create meaningful load.\n\n[L1414] ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n[L1415] 21. FIRST IMPLEMENTATION / PROVING SEQUENCE\n[L1416] ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n[L1418] Recommended progression:\n\n[L1420] PHASE 0 — CONTRACT\n\n[L1422] Define minimal normalized event schema.\n\n[L1424] PHASE 1 — AUDIO SOFTWARE PROOF\n\n[L1426] Trigger:\n\n[L1428] VOICE_ACTIVE\n\n[L1430] Action:\n\n[L1432] capture music level\n[L1433] → duck\n[L1434] → restore after VOICE_IDLE\n\n[L1436] No hardware required.\n\n[L1438] PHASE 2 — SIMPLE PHYSICAL CONTROL\n\n[L1440] Use a cheap MIDI fader/knob/button.\n\nMap:\n\n[L1444] physical fader\n[L1445] → AUDIO_SET\n\n[L1447] button\n[L1448] → AUDIO_DUCK / RESTORE\n\n[L1450] PHASE 3 — NON-AUDIO ORCHESTRATION\n\n[L1452] Prove one control against myDon.\n\n[L1454] Example:\n\n[L1456] button / cue\n[L1457] → FOCUS_SEAT 6 / Luce\n\nor:\n\n[L1461] encoder\n[L1462] → NEXT_HANDOFF\n\n[L1464] PHASE 4 — MIXER VIEW\n\n[L1466] Build optional visual representation of physical controls and current state.\n\n[L1468] PHASE 5 — GESTURE INPUT\n\n[L1470] Evaluate:\n\n[L1472] - ring;\n[L1473] - glove;\n[L1474] - camera;\n[L1475] - other device.\n\n[L1477] Map into same event contract.\n\n[L1479] PHASE 6 — MULTIMODAL COMBINATION\n\n[L1481] Potential future:\n\n[L1483] voice + gesture\n[L1484] gesture + context\n[L1485] physical cue + route\n[L1486] physical control + Cable Car transport\n\n[L1488] Only after simpler primitives are proven.\n\n[L1490] ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n[L1491] 22. FAILURE / SAFETY BEHAVIOR\n[L1492] ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────