], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "9904f16e-7b23-4770-9681-36a64b97cfbe", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790261080.108698, "updated_at": 1790264290.832455, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "## GCE Google Drive Recon — Non-GCE Audit\n\n**Mode:** READ-ONLY  \n**Authority:** Don  \n**Changes made:** **None**  \n**Confidence:** **97% — PROCEED**\n\nThis matches the Cable Car sequencing: recon first, identify loose/random artifacts, and **do not clean during recon without Don approval**. fileciteturn0file0L681-L693\n\nThe Drive root is currently mixing **GCE**, **personal operating material**, **job search**, **travel**, **older businesses/projects**, and **legacy loose work files**. That is the main hygiene problem.\n\n### 1. Legitimate non-GCE domains that already have folders\n\nThese are not random garbage. They are coherent domains that should remain **outside GCE**, although we can later decide where they belong structurally.\n\n| Root folder | Recon finding | Assessment |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Personal Operating Context** | 7 organized subfolders covering identity/profile, Vegas/budget, Mexico/family/relocation, relationships, personal systems, family ecosystem | **KEEP — coherent personal domain** |\n| **Job Search** | Contains `Resume Family 2026-09-03` with 4 resume families: ERP Leadership, NetSuite Manufacturing/Contract, AI Systems/Automation, targeted experimental variants | **KEEP — coherent job-search domain** |\n| **Vegas Itinerary** | 3 living-plan Docs: travel options, food/exercise/daily rhythm, September itinerary & cash flow | **KEEP — coherent travel/personal domain** |\n| **CasaCompanion** | `heroes`, shared `CasaCompanion`, and `videos` subfolders | **KEEP / REVIEW — separate project estate** |\n| **Simple Balance** | Root folder, shared; no immediate children returned in this pass | **LEGACY / REVIEW** |\n| **Simple balance shared mp3s** | Shared folder; no immediate children returned | **LEGACY / REVIEW** |\n| **MRP** | Empty at first level | **LIKELY ARCHIVE/DELETE CANDIDATE**, pending confirmation |\n| **Tasker** | Contains `data` folder | **LEGACY / REVIEW** |\n| **Colab Notebooks** | Empty at first level | **LIKELY ARCHIVE/DELETE CANDIDATE** |\n| **@Capacity** | Contains `Capacity Studios Draft Intial Startup Budget` Sheet | **LEGACY BUSINESS / KEEP OR ARCHIVE** |\n\nThe important structural point: **Personal**, **Job Search**, **Vegas**, and likely **CasaCompanion** are not GCE clutter. They are independent estates and should not be absorbed into the GCE folder.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Loose non-GCE files sitting directly in Drive root\n\nThis is where the clutter becomes obvious.\n\n### Current job-search material\n\nThese are legitimate current documents, but they are sitting loose at root instead of inside **Job Search**:\n\n- `RF-SMART — 10AM Interview Live Sidecar — 2026-09-23`\n- `RF-SMART — Interview Sidecar — Strategy & Functional Experience Map — 2026-09-22`\n- `A-Tex — Friday CFO Interview Sidecar — Strategy & Functional Experience Map — 2026-09-22`\n- `A-Tex / Clavis — Friday CFO Interview — Waves 2 & 3 Working Artifact — 2026-09-21`\n- `A-Tex / Clavis — Director ERP & Enterprise Systems — Friday CFO Interview Prep — 2026-09-20`\n- `Job Search Status & Interview Prep`\n\n**Assessment:** **KEEP, but root-placement is wrong.** These have an obvious natural home under `Job Search`.\n\n---\n\n### Personal / family material\n\nLoose at root:\n\n- `Get Back to Family — Mexico Work Infrastructure — Living Plan`\n\nThere is already a **Personal Operating Context → 03_Mexico_Family_and_Relocation** structure.\n\n**Assessment:** **KEEP, likely misplaced.**\n\nAlso:\n\n- `Gladys — Family Ecosystem Placeholder`\n\nThere is already a `06_Family_Ecosystem_Profiles` folder.\n\n**Assessment:** likely **misplaced / placeholder cleanup candidate**, but I would inspect it before deleting because the title suggests it may have intentional structural meaning.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Obvious temporary/test residue\n\nThese are the strongest immediate clutter candidates:\n\n- `placeholder temp`\n- `IGNORE_TEMP_DELETE_LATER`\n- `TEMP`\n- `Untitled spreadsheet`\n\nThese are almost textbook cleanup residue.\n\n### My classification\n\n**High-confidence deletion-review queue:**\n\n`placeholder temp`  \n`IGNORE_TEMP_DELETE_LATER`  \n`TEMP`  \n`Untitled spreadsheet`\n\nI have **not deleted anything**.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Legacy professional / NetSuite / business material loose at root\n\nThere is also a block of older work product unrelated to GCE:\n\n- `Portal_Integration_Meeting_Agenda.docx` — Dec 2025\n- `Ode_Cloud_NetSuite_Contract_Pricing.xlsx` — Dec 2025\n- `97205720.pdf` — June 2025, opaque filename\n- `Work` — Sept 2023\n- `ScpCatalogImportTemplate.xlsx` — June 2020\n- `ScpItemImportTemplate_v1`\n- `ScpItemImportTemplate_v1.xlsx`\n\nThese look like **legacy NetSuite/professional artifacts**, not current GCE material.\n\nThe interesting one is the pair:\n\n- `ScpItemImportTemplate_v1`\n- `ScpItemImportTemplate_v1.xlsx`\n\nThat smells like a Google-converted/native version plus the original Excel file, so it is a **possible duplicate family**, but I would verify content before calling either redundant.\n\n`97205720.pdf` is especially worth inspecting because the filename tells us nothing. Until opened, its classification is **UNKNOWN LEGACY**.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Other loose non-GCE material\n\n### Sports / analytics\n\n- `NBA % Today` — Google Sheet from 2022\n\nThis predates the current GCE/Edge Crew estate and is sitting loose at root.\n\n**Assessment:** **legacy sports-analysis artifact**. Could be historical methodology or disposable old work; needs a quick content check before disposition.\n\n### Capacity Studios\n\n`@Capacity` contains:\n\n- `Capacity Studios Draft Intial Startup Budget`\n\nThat is coherent enough to remain its own historical project/business folder.\n\n**Assessment:** not root clutter beyond the folder itself; probably **archive estate**, not deletion candidate.\n\n---\n\n# 6. Root items I am **not** counting as non-GCE\n\nThere is a proper root folder:\n\n**`GCE`**\n\nThere are also loose root artifacts that are clearly GCE-related, including:\n\n- `GCE Mobile Compute Phone Exploration — 2026-09-23`\n- `GCE_SESSION_ANCHOR_2026-09-06_OPERATIONAL_TEAM_LOCK`\n- `EC8_Edge_Crew_Quant_MLB_Picks_2026-09-06_Falcon_Range_1`\n\nThose are a **different cleanup problem**: they are GCE material sitting outside the intended GCE estate. I excluded them from this non-GCE audit, but they absolutely belong in the later GCE reconciliation pass.\n\nThat distinction matters because the Cable Car design specifically says the transport lane should not pollute framework authority folders, project canon, or random Drive root. fileciteturn0file0L326-L354\n\n---\n\n# Coda audit finding\n\nThe Drive does **not** primarily have a “too many files” problem.\n\nIt has a **domain-boundary problem**.\n\nThe root currently serves simultaneously as:\n\n**GCE workspace + job-search desktop + personal notebook + travel folder + old NetSuite filing cabinet + former-business archive + scratchpad.**\n\nThat is exactly what we should fix before introducing `GCE_CABLE_CAR`, because otherwise Cable Car traffic gets dumped into an already ambiguous operating surface.\n\n### Proposed cleanup buckets\n\nI would classify the non-GCE estate into four buckets:\n\n1. **ACTIVE / KEEP**\n   - Personal Operating Context\n   - Job Search\n   - Vegas Itinerary\n   - CasaCompanion\n\n2. **KEEP BUT MOVE OFF ROOT**\n   - six current interview/job-search Docs\n   - Mexico living-plan Doc\n   - possibly Gladys placeholder\n\n3. **LEGACY ARCHIVE**\n   - Simple Balance\n   - Simple Balance shared MP3s\n   - @Capacity\n   - Tasker\n   - old Portal/Ode/NetSuite work\n   - NBA sheet\n   - possibly MRP and Colab\n\n4. **DELETE-REVIEW**\n   - `placeholder temp`\n   - `IGNORE_TEMP_DELETE_LATER`\n   - `TEMP`\n   - `Untitled spreadsheet`\n\n**No writes performed.**\n\nMy next pass should be surgical: **inspect the four obvious temp artifacts plus the opaque/legacy items (`97205720.pdf`, MRP, Colab, Tasker, NBA sheet) and give you an actual `KEEP / ARCHIVE / DELETE` disposition list before we touch anything.**", "text_chars": 7824, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": ["97205720.pdf", "Ode_Cloud_NetSuite_Contract_Pricing.xlsx", "Portal_Integration_Meeting_Agenda.docx", "ScpCatalogImportTemplate.xlsx", "ScpItemImportTemplate_v1.xlsx"], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "bcdf0b9e-aa28-4872-a87b-9d8f9be55ee6", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790261350.727, "updated_at": 1790261453.297726, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Don. Give Don the rundown by size, by folder. I visit— we gotta free up space.  And what's holding us up? ", "text_chars": 106, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "d873c9bf-edec-4888-bd7e-87801c81486d", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790261358.172928, "updated_at": 1790261358.172928, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "model_editable_context", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "3d9af2ee-9841-4d14-ac74-315daa25b8f8", "role": "assistan