VOLVE** | `03_PROJECTS/EC8_Edge_Crew` |\n| `GCE/06_Frozen_State_and_Archive` | **KEEP / restructure** | `GCE/06_FROZEN_STATE_AND_ARCHIVE` |\n| `Legacy_*` folders already inside archive | **KEEP HISTORICAL** | appropriate archive branches |\n| no current Drive equivalent | **CREATE** | `00_START_HERE` |\n| no current Drive equivalent | **CREATE** | `02_GCE_IDENTITY` |\n| no current Drive equivalent | **CREATE** | `04_GCE_DON` |\n| no current Drive equivalent | **CREATE** | `05_REGISTRIES` |\n\nThe important correction from our earlier discussion is that **Drive can keep the `GCE/` wrapper**. The Razer does not need one because those are filesystem operating roots; Drive benefits from one because it separates the whole GCE estate from `Job Search`, `Vegas Itinerary`, `Personal Operating Context`, `CasaCompanion`, etc.\n\nSo we end up with:\n\n```text\nMy Drive/\n│\n├── GCE/\n│   ├── 00_START_HERE/\n│   ├── 01_GCE_ORG/\n│   ├── 02_GCE_IDENTITY/\n│   ├── 03_PROJECTS/\n│   ├── 04_GCE_DON/\n│   ├── 05_REGISTRIES/\n│   └── 06_FROZEN_STATE_AND_ARCHIVE/\n│\n├── Job Search/\n├── Personal Operating Context/\n├── Vegas Itinerary/\n├── CasaCompanion/\n└── 01_OFFLOAD_REVIEW_LEGACY_MISC_2026-09-24/\n```\n\nThat resolves the apparent contradiction nicely:\n\n**Local**\n```text\nGCE_ORG\nGCE_IDENTITY\nGCE_DON\nProjects\n```\n\n**Drive**\n```text\nGCE/\n  01_GCE_ORG\n  02_GCE_IDENTITY\n  03_PROJECTS\n  04_GCE_DON\n```\n\nSame authority geometry. Different storage container.\n\n### One adjustment I strongly agree with\n\nYour **project spine** should become standard:\n\n```text\n00_CURRENT/\n01_HANDOFFS/\n02_WORK/\n03_REGISTRY/\n04_DECISIONS/\n90_HISTORICAL/\n```\n\nThat is much cleaner than inventing a bespoke hierarchy every time. Project-specific functional folders can sit **alongside** that spine:\n\n```text\nGCE_Stack/\n├── 00_CURRENT/\n├── 01_HANDOFFS/\n├── 02_WORK/\n├── 03_REGISTRY/\n├── 04_DECISIONS/\n│\n├── VoiceBridge/\n├── Web_Bridge/\n├── Transport/\n├── State_Sync/\n├── Runtime_Plumbing/\n├── Local_Services/\n├── APIs_Adapters/\n├── Dev_Utilities/\n├── Command_Center_Tech/\n├── Walking_Capture/\n│\n└── 90_HISTORICAL/\n```\n\nThat avoids the slight problem in the first draft where numbered functional folders were effectively replacing the universal project spine.\n\nAnd **Cable Car** then has an obvious project-owned home:\n\n```text\nGCE/\n└── 03_PROJECTS/\n    └── GCE_Stack/\n        └── Transport/\n            └── Cable_Car/\n```\n\nwhile any organizational transport **standard/policy** belongs under ORG, and the actual live external exchange folders can remain a deliberately isolated transport surface.\n\nThat gives us the three-way separation we need:\n\n> **ORG governs it → PROJECT implements it → CABLE CAR transports it.**\n\nThat is the architecture I’d lock before the migration pass.", "text_chars": 4251, "code_blocks": 6, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "030d9560-1f1f-427e-865a-832ad4220096", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790266779.402, "updated_at": 1790267345.237823, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "yes approved implemnet in google driver", "text_chars": 39, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "c3d0de6d-659f-44bd-84c1-c9d45fdbfe5b", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790266802.210607, "updated_at": 1790266802.210607, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Approved. I’m implementing the **Drive target taxonomy in place** now: create the missing top-level GCE branches, normalize the existing ones, then mig