alse, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "15ac11e0-cbed-4cee-8338-480a834347b8", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790281920.172279, "updated_at": 1790281921.011972, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Absolutely. I’m freezing this as a **buildable architecture + methodology spec**, not a brainstorm: transport contract, state machine, filesystem/Drive contract, failure semantics, exactly-once rules, observability, and then a **Nico slice plan with acceptance gates**.", "text_chars": 269, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "4301eb3d-69dc-4c9d-8084-0878c19f3c56", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790281924.088927, "updated_at": 1790281924.088927, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "reasoning_recap", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "f78e584a-4d68-41d9-9f4c-b6e29854630d", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790281924.092475, "updated_at": 1790282084.844043, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Yes. This is the right point to stop talking about Cable Car conceptually and hand Nico a **bounded implementation contract**.\n\n:::writing{variant=\"document\" id=\"58421\" title=\"GCE Cable Car — Architecture, Methodology, and Nico Build Specification\"}\n# GCE CABLE CAR\n## Architecture, Methodology, and Nico Build Specification\n\n**Authority:** Don  \n**Architecture / Methodology:** Coda  \n**Implementation Seat:** Nico  \n**Verification Seat:** Luce  \n**Operations / Routing:** Talon  \n**Transport Identity:** Pigeon  \n**Project:** GCE Stack  \n**Canonical Project Home:** `GCE / 03_PROJECTS / GCE_Stack / Transport / Cable_Car`  \n**Local Project Context:** `C:\\Users\\Dekan AI Brother\\GCE_DON\\command-center\\` and associated GCE Stack runtime surfaces  \n**Status:** APPROVED FOR IMPLEMENTATION SPEC  \n**Build Mode:** Controlled slices; no architecture invention by implementation seat  \n**Confidence:** 98%\n\n---\n\n# 1. PURPOSE\n\nCable Car provides a reliable external transport path between Don/Coda operating in ChatGPT or another external interface and the local GCE operating estate.\n\nIt exists to eliminate Don acting as the clipboard bus between:\n\n```text\nExternal Don / Coda\n        ↓\nGoogle Drive exchange\n        ↓\nPigeon transport\n        ↓\nLocal GCE intake\n        ↓\nmyDon routing\n        ↓\nSeat execution\n        ↓\nReturn path\n        ↓\nExternal Don / Coda\n```\n\nCable Car is a **transport subsystem**.\n\nIt is not:\n\n- an orchestrator;\n- a seat selector;\n- an architecture engine;\n- an interpretation engine;\n- a project authority;\n- a model router;\n- a replacement for myDon;\n- a replacement for the local inbox;\n- a replacement for Google Drive governance.\n\nCanonical doctrine:\n\n```text\nTRANSPORT != INTERPRETER\nTRANSPORT != AUTHORITY\nPATH != COURIER\nMODEL != SEAT\nIDENTITY != ROLE != MODEL != RUNTIME != PROVIDER\n```\n\n**Cable Car = PATH.**\n\n**Pigeon = COURIER.**\n\n---\n\n# 2. OWNERSHIP BOUNDARIES\n\n## 2.1 Google Drive\n\nGoogle Drive is the **external exchange and durable staging surface**.\n\nIt is appropriate for:\n\n- external inbound handoffs;\n- outbound completed returns;\n- long payloads;\n- cross-device exchange;\n- durable transport artifacts;\n- human inspection;\n- restart-safe exchange state.\n\nGoogle Drive is **not the live GCE execution queue**.\n\n---\n\n## 2.2 Local inbox\n\nThe local inbox remains the canonical execution intake queue.\n\nExisting inbox-MCP V1 behavior is preserved.\n\nCable Car must terminate inbound delivery into the existing local intake structure rather than creating a second local queue architecture.\n\n---\n\n## 2.3 `_shared`\n\n`_shared` remains the canonical unrouted local pool.\n\nInbound Cable Car material lands here unless an already-approved lower-level transport contract explicitly states otherwise.\n\nCable Car does not decide the final execution seat.\n\n---\n\n## 2.4 myDon\n\nmyDon owns controlled routing after local intake.\n\nmyDon may:\n\n- inspect routing metadata;\n- expose items to Don;\n- apply Don-approved routing;\n- preserve routing/audit residue.\n\nmyDon does not become the transport implementation.\n\n---\n\n## 2.5 Don\n\nDon remains final routing authority.\n\nCable Car may carry a requested target or routing hint, but it must never silently convert that hint into authority.\n\n---\n\n# 3. TARGET END-TO-END FLOW\n\nCanonical round-trip:\n\n```text\n1. Coda / Don creates handoff\n        ↓\n2. Handoff enters Drive inbound\n        ↓\n3. Pigeon detects candidate\n        ↓\n4. Pigeon validates transport contract\n        ↓\n5. Pigeon claims item\n        ↓\n6. Local copy is written atomically\n        ↓\n7. Local item enters _shared\n        ↓\n8. myDon surfaces item\n        ↓\n9. Don routes item\n        ↓\n10. Seat receives item\n        ↓\n11. Seat executes\n        ↓\n12. Seat produces return artifact\n        ↓\n13. Pigeon detects outbound return\n        ↓\n14. Pigeon transports return to Drive\n        ↓\n15. Drive marks completed delivery\n        ↓\n16. Coda / Don reads result\n```\n\nThe **same `HANDOFF_ID` survives the entire round trip**.\n\n---\n\n# 4. DRIVE TRANSPORT ESTATE\n\nWithin:\n\n```text\nGCE/\n└── 03_PROJECTS/\n    └── GCE_Stack/\n        └── Transport/\n            └── Cable_Car/\n```\n\ncreate the transport runtime estate:\n\n```text\nCable_Car/\n│\n├── 00_CURRENT/\n│   ├── README.md\n│   ├── CABLE_CAR_CONTRACT.md\n│   └── CURRENT_VERSION.json\n│\n├── 01_INBOUND_TO_GCE/\n│\n├── 02_OUTBOUND_FROM_GCE/\n│\n├── 03_IN_FLIGHT/\n│\n├── 04_ACKNOWLEDGED/\n│\n├── 05_COMPLETED/\n│\n├── 90_FAILED/\n│\n├── 98_QUARANTINE/\n│\n└── 99_ARCHIVE/\n```\n\nThe numbering differs slightly from the early conceptual draft because `00_CURRENT` is now part of the standardized project methodology.\n\nRuntime meaning:\n\n### `01_INBOUND_TO_GCE`\n\nNew externally-created transport candidates.\n\nPigeon may inspect this folder.\n\nNo execution occurs here.\n\n### `02_OUTBOUND_FROM_GCE`\n\nLocal return artifacts awaiting delivery back to external Drive consumers.\n\n### `03_IN_FLIGHT`\n\nArtifacts claimed by a Pigeon process but not yet fully committed at the destination.\n\nThis is a transport state, not an execution state.\n\n### `04_ACKNOWLEDGED`\n\nInbound artifacts successfully materialized into the local canonical intake estate.\n\nAcknowledged means:\n\n> transport delivery completed successfully.\n\nIt does **not** mean:\n\n> seat work completed.\n\n### `05_COMPLETED`\n\nOutbound result successfully transported and committed.\n\n### `90_FAILED`\n\nHard transport failures after retry policy is exhausted.\n\n### `98_QUARANTINE`\n\nMalformed, unsafe, conflicting, duplicate-with-conflict, or otherwise non-routable transport inputs.\n\n### `99_ARCHIVE`\n\nHistorical transport records eligible for cold retention.\n\n---\n\n# 5. HANDOFF IDENTITY CONTRACT\n\nCanonical transport identity:\n\n```text\nHANDOFF_ID\n```\n\nThe physical filename remains the canonical external identity carrier.\n\nInternal JSON metadata may repeat that value, but if there is a disagreement:\n\n```text\nFILENAME HANDOFF ID > INTERNAL JSON HANDOFF ID\n```\n\nThe disagreement must be logged.\n\nThe transport process must never silently rename an inbound handoff into a different logical identity.\n\nRecommended filename:\n\n```text\nGCE_HANDOFF_<HANDOFF_ID>.json\n```\n\nExample:\n\n```text\nGCE_HANDOFF_20260924T203100Z_CODA_LUCE_001.json\n```\n\nAssociated payloads may use:\n\n```text\nGCE_HANDOFF_20260924T203100Z_CODA_LUCE_001.md\nGCE_HANDOFF_20260924T203100Z_CODA_LUCE_001.zip\n```\n\nAll files belonging to one transfer share the same base `HANDOFF_ID`.\n\n---\n\n# 6. ENVELOPE CONTRACT\n\nVersion 1 envelope:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"schema\": \"gce.cable_car.handoff\",\n  \"schema_version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"handoff_id\": \"20260924T203100Z_CODA_LUCE_001\",\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-09-24T20:31:00Z\",\n  \"created_by\": {\n    \"identity\": \"Coda\",\n    \"authority\": \"Don\"\n  },\n  \"direction\": \"INBOUND_TO_GCE\",\n  \"project\": \"GCE_Stack\",\n  \"requested_destination\": {\n    \"seat\": \"Luce\",\n    \"type\": \"ROUTING_HINT\"\n  },\n  \"payload\": {\n    \"primary_file\": \"GCE_HANDOFF_20260924T203100Z_CODA_LUCE_001.md\",\n    \"attachments\": [],\n    \"sha256\": {}\n  },\n  \"transport\": {\n    \"requires_ack\": true,\n    \"priority\": \"NORMAL\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n# 7. AUTHORITY RULE FOR `requested_destination`\n\n`requested_destination` is a **routing hint** unless a future explicitly-approved authority contract states otherwise.\n\nPigeon may transport the field.\n\nPigeon may not interpret it as authorization.\n\nTherefore:\n\n```text\nrequested_destination.seat = Luce\n```\n\ndoes not mean:\n\n```text\nPigeon routes directly to Luce inbox\n```\n\nVersion 1 remains:\n\n```text\nDrive\n→ Pigeon\n→ local _shared\n→ myDon\n→ Don-approved route\n```\n\nThis prevents transport from quietly acquiring orchestration authority.\n\n---\n\n# 8. PAYLOAD RULES\n\nV1 supported payload types:\n\n```text\n.json\n.md\n.txt\n.zip\n```\n\nAdditional binary types can be transported as attachments but are not interpreted by Pigeon.\n\nPigeon may:\n\n- calculate hash;\n- verify filename;\n- verify size;\n- verify manifest;\n- copy bytes;\n- move transport state.\n\nPigeon may not:\n\n- summarize;\n- rewrite;\n- modify instructions;\n- interpret project intent;\n- extract architecture;\n- choose a seat;\n- alter authority.\n\n---\n\n# 9. ATOMICITY CONTRACT\n\nNo consumer may observe a partially-written local handoff.\n\nTherefore local materialization uses:\n\n```text\nwrite temp\n→ fsync/close\n→ verify hash\n→ atomic rename\n```\n\nExample:\n\n```text\n_shared/.incoming/<HANDOFF_ID>.tmp\n```\n\nbecomes:\n\n```text\n_shared/<HANDOFF_ID>.json\n```\n\nonly after verification.\n\nThe equivalent rule applies to outbound staging.\n\n---\n\n# 10. EXACTLY-ONCE EFFECT SEMANTICS\n\nCable Car does not need to pretend distributed storage provides magical exactly-once delivery.\n\nInstead it implements:\n\n> **at-least-once observation + idempotent processing = exactly-once effect.**\n\nEvery `HANDOFF_ID` must have a durable local transport record.\n\nExample:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"handoff_id\": \"...\",\n  \"direction\": \"INBOUND_TO_GCE\",\n  \"state\": \"ACKNOWLEDGED\",\n  \"source_hash\": \"...\",\n  \"destination_hash\": \"...\",\n  \"first_seen_at\": \"...\",\n  \"claimed_at\": \"...\",\n  \"completed_at\": \"...\",\n  \"attempts\": 1\n}\n```\n\nIf Pigeon sees the same `HANDOFF_ID` again with the same hash:\n\n```text\nNO SECOND DELIVERY\n```\n\nRecord:\n\n```text\nDUPLICATE_SAME_CONTENT\n```\n\nIf it sees the same `HANDOFF_ID` with a different hash:\n\n```text\nDO NOT OVERWRITE\n```\n\nMove candidate to:\n\n```text\n98_QUARANTINE\n```\n\nRecord:\n\n```text\nDUPLICATE_ID_CONTENT_CONFLICT\n```\n\nThis is a hard invariant.\n\n---\n\n# 11. TRANSPORT STATE MACHINE\n\nInbound:\n\n```text\nDISCOVERED\n    ↓\nVALIDATING\n    ↓\nCLAIMED\n    ↓\nCOPYING\n    ↓\nVERIFYING\n    ↓\nACKNOWLEDGED\n```\n\nError exits:\n\n```text\nVALIDATING → QUARANTINED\nCLAIMED → RETRYABLE_FAILURE\nCOPYING → RETRYABLE_FAILURE\nVERIFYING → RETRYABLE_FAILURE\nRETRYABLE_FAILURE → CLAIMED\nRETRYABLE_FAILURE → FAILED\n```\n\nOutbound:\n\n```text\nDISCOVERED\n    ↓\nVALIDATING\n    ↓\nCLAIMED\n    ↓\nUPLOADING\n    ↓\nVERIFYING\n    ↓\nCOMPLETED\n```\n\n---\n\n# 12. CLAIMING / CONCURRENCY\n\nOnly one Pigeon worker may own a transfer at a time.\n\nClaiming must be represented durably.\n\nThe implementation may use a local lock/ledger combined with Drive state movement.\n\nRecommended sequence:\n\n```text\ndiscover inbound item\n→ check ledger\n→ create claim record\n→ move Drive artifact INBOUND → IN_FLIGHT\n→ confirm move\n→ process\n```\n\nIf two workers observe the same item:\n\n- one claim succeeds;\n- the other sees existing ownership;\n- second worker exits cleanly.\n\nNo duplicate local delivery.\n\n---\n\n# 13. RESTART SAFETY\n\nA restart may occur at every line of the process.\n\nTherefore every transition must be recoverable from durable state.\n\nAt startup Pigeon reconciles:\n\n```text\n03_IN_FLIGHT\n+\nlocal transport ledger\n+\ndestination existence\n+\nhash state\n```\n\nExamples:\n\n### Case A\n\nDrive says `IN_FLIGHT`.\n\nLedger says `COPYING`.\n\nDestination absent.\n\nAction:\n\n```text\nresume copy\n```\n\n### Case B\n\nDrive says `IN_FLIGHT`.\n\nDestination exists.\n\nHashes match.\n\nAction:\n\n```text\nfinish acknowledgement\n```\n\n### Case C\n\nDrive says `INBOUND`.\n\nLedger says `ACKNOWLEDGED`.\n\nAction:\n\n```text\ndo not redeliver\nreconcile Drive state\n```\n\n### Case D\n\nDestination exists with same HANDOFF_ID but different hash.\n\nAction:\n\n```text\nquarantine\ndo not overwrite\n```\n\nRestart safety is part of V1 acceptance, not a later enhancement.\n\n---\n\n# 14. LOCAL STATE STORE\n\nRecommended V1 durable transport state:\n\n```text\n<GCE Stack runtime>/\ncable_car/\n├── state/\n│   ├── cable_car.sqlite\n│   └── locks/\n├── logs/\n├── quarantine/\n└── config/\n```\n\nSQLite is preferred over loose JSON state because we need:\n\n- unique `handoff_id`;\n- state transitions;\n- retry count;\n- hash fields;\n- timestamps;\n- source/destination paths;\n- indexed reconciliation;\n- transaction safety.\n\nMinimum tables:\n\n```text\ntransfers\nevents\n```\n\n`transfers`:\n\n```text\nhandoff_id PRIMARY KEY\ndirection\nstate\nsource_ref\ndestination_ref\nsource_hash\ndestination_hash\nattempt_count\nfirst_seen_at\nclaimed_at\ncompleted_at\nlast_error\n```\n\n`events`:\n\n```text\nevent_id\nhandoff_id\ntimestamp\nevent_type\nfrom_state\nto_state\ndetail\n```\n\nThe event table is append-only.\n\n---\n\n# 15. OBSERVABILITY\n\nEvery transfer gets a machine-readable event trail.\n\nMinimum event types:\n\n```text\nDISCOVERED\nVALIDATION_STARTED\nVALIDATION_PASSED\nVALIDATION_FAILED\nCLAIMED\nCOPY_STARTED\nCOPY_COMPLETED\nHASH_VERIFIED\nACKNOWLEDGED\nUPLOAD_STARTED\nUPLOAD_COMPLETED\nCOMPLETED\nRETRY_SCHEDULED\nQUARANTINED\nFAILED\nDUPLICATE_IGNORED\nCONFLICT_DETECTED\nRECOVERY_STARTED\nRECOVERY_COMPLETED\n```\n\nConsole logs must always include:\n\n```text\ntimestamp\nhandoff_id\ndirection\nevent\nstate\n```\n\nNo secrets or tokens in logs.\n\n---\n\n# 16. FAILURE POLICY\n\nFailures divide into three classes.\n\n## RETRYABLE\n\nExamples:\n\n- temporary Drive API error;\n- network interruption;\n- locked local file;\n- transient read failure.\n\nPolicy:\n\n```text\nretry with bounded exponential backoff\n```\n\nExample:\n\n```text\n5 sec\n15 sec\n60 sec\n5 min\n15 min\n```\n\nAfter configured exhaustion:\n\n```text\n90_FAILED\n```\n\n---\n\n## QUARANTINE\n\nExamples:\n\n- malformed envelope;\n- invalid filename;\n- missing payload;\n- hash disagreement;\n- duplicate ID with changed content;\n- path traversal attempt;\n- unsupported contract version.\n\nAction:\n\n```text\n98_QUARANTINE\n```\n\nNo automatic retry until condition changes or human action occurs.\n\n---\n\n## FATAL CONFIGURATION\n\nExamples:\n\n- Drive root unavailable;\n- canonical local inbox missing;\n- invalid seat registry dependency;\n- state DB cannot open.\n\nPigeon must fail closed.\n\nIt must not improvise alternative paths.\n\n---\n\n# 17. SECURITY INVARIANTS\n\nPigeon must reject:\n\n```text\n../\n..\\\nabsolute foreign paths\nUNC injection\ndrive-letter injection from payload metadata\nsymlink escape\ninvalid filename characters\nunexpected executable payload behavior\n```\n\nPayload contents are treated as data.\n\nPigeon never executes transported files.\n\nCredentials remain outside transported artifacts.\n\nNo API key, bearer token, OAuth refresh token, or secret may be persisted in:\n\n```text\nDrive envelope\ntransport event log\nSQLite event detail\nhandoff payload generated by Pigeon\n```\n\n---\n\n# 18. CONFIGURATION\n\nNo important path may be hard-coded throughout implementation.\n\nOne config surface owns:\n\n```text\ndrive root IDs\nDrive transport folder IDs\nlocal _shared path\nlocal outbound path\nstate database path\npoll interval\nretry limits\nsupported schema versions\nmax payload size\n```\n\nExample conceptual config:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"schema_version\": 1,\n  \"poll_seconds\": 15,\n  \"local_shared_path\": \"...\",\n  \"state_db\": \"...\",\n  \"max_payload_mb\": 250,\n  \"supported_handoff_versions\": [\"1.0\"]\n}\n```\n\nFolder IDs, not folder-name searches, should be preferred once installation/bootstrap has resolved them.\n\n---\n\n# 19. WATCHER METHOD\n\nV1 should favor boring reliability over cleverness.\n\nRecommended:\n\n```text\npolling watcher\n```\n\nrather than trying to begin with webhook complexity.\n\nV1 polling loop:\n\n```text\npoll\n→ discover\n→ reconcile\n→ process bounded batch\n→ sleep\n```\n\nIt must be safe to run repeatedly.\n\nFuture versions may replace or augment polling without changing the handoff contract.\n\n---\n\n# 20. PIGEON IMPLEMENTATION BOUNDARY\n\nPigeon owns:\n\n```text\ndiscovery\nvalidation\nclaim\ntransport\nhash verification\ntransport state\nretry\nacknowledgement\nreturn transport\nrecovery\ntransport audit\n```\n\nPigeon does not own:\n\n```text\nseat selection\nprompt rewriting\nproject interpretation\narchitecture\nauthority\nmodel selection\nexecution\nverification judgment\n```\n\n---\n\n# 21. MYDON INTEGRATION BOUNDARY\n\nV1 integration should be deliberately thin.\n\nCable Car only needs to guarantee:\n\n```text\nvalid handoff appears exactly once in canonical _shared\n```\n\nExisting routing machinery remains responsible after that point.\n\nDo not redesign myDon during Cable Car V1.\n\nDo not rewrite inbox-MCP.\n\nDo not introduce a second routing engine.\n\n---\n\n# 22. OUTBOUND RETURN CONTRACT\n\nA return uses the same `HANDOFF_ID`.\n\nRecommended result envelope:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"schema\": \"gce.cable_car.return\",\n  \"schema_version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"handoff_id\": \"...\",\n  \"completed_at\": \"...\",\n  \"completed_by\": {\n    \"seat\": \"Luce\"\n  },\n  \"status\": \"COMPLETE\",\n  \"artifacts\": [],\n  \"summary_file\": \"...\",\n  \"hashes\": {}\n}\n```\n\nPigeon transports it.\n\nPigeon does not evaluate whether the return is good.\n\nThat belongs to the execution/verification methodology.\n\n---\n\n# 23. THE PROVING TEST\n\nV1 is not accepted until one full live proving test succeeds:\n\n```text\nCoda\n↓\nDrive\n↓\nPigeon\n↓\nlocal _shared\n↓\nmyDon\n↓\nDon routes\n↓\nLuce\n↓\nLuce returns artifact\n↓\nPigeon\n↓\nDrive\n↓\nCoda\n```\n\nRequired properties:\n\n1. exactly one inbound local delivery;\n2. same `HANDOFF_ID` through the complete round trip;\n3. no filename identity mutation;\n4. correct hashes;\n5. no manual file copy by Don;\n6. restart Pigeon during the transfer;\n7. process resumes safely;\n8. no duplicate delivery after restart;\n9. return arrives exactly once in effect;\n10. complete event history exists.\n\nIf any of those fail:\n\n```text\nV1 NOT CERTIFIED\n```\n\n---\n\n# 24. NICO BUILD METHODOLOGY\n\nNico does not build the entire system in one pass.\n\nUse bounded slices.\n\n## SLICE 0 — RECON / NO BUILD\n\nNico must establish:\n\n- exact local `_shared` path;\n- exact outbound return path;\n- relevant existing inbox-MCP interfaces;\n- current myDon intake assumptions;\n- runtime language/environment;\n- existing utilities that can be reused;\n- current GCE Stack project structure;\n- Drive folder IDs for Cable Car.\n\nDeliverable:\n\n```text\nCABLE_CAR_RECON.md\n```\n\nNo architecture change.\n\nNo writes outside the dedicated project/runtime area.\n\n**Gate:** Coda/Don review.\n\n---\n\n## SLICE 1 — CORE CONTRACT + STATE ENGINE\n\nBuild:\n\n- schema types;\n- filename parser;\n- handoff ID validation;\n- SHA-256 utilities;\n- SQLite schema;\n- state transitions;\n- event ledger;\n- idempotency rules;\n- duplicate/conflict handling.\n\nNo Drive watcher yet.\n\nTests must prove:\n\n```text\nsame ID + same hash = ignored duplicate\nsame ID + different hash = conflict\ninvalid transition = rejected\nevent history append-only\n```\n\n**Gate:** unit suite green.\n\n---\n\n## SLICE 2 — LOCAL ATOMIC DELIVERY\n\nBuild:\n\n- staging directory;\n- atomic local write;\n- verification;\n- `_shared` commit;\n- simulated inbound files.\n\nNo Google Drive connection required for acceptance.\n\nTests:\n\n- crash before rename;\n- crash after copy but before ledger commit;\n- preexisting same handoff;\n- conflicting destination;\n- partial temp file.\n\n**Gate:** restart-safe local delivery proven.\n\n---\n\n## SLICE 3 — DRIVE INBOUND ADAPTER\n\nBuild:\n\n```text\nDrive discovery\nDrive claim\nINBOUND → IN_FLIGHT\ndownload\nlocal atomic delivery\nIN_FLIGHT → ACKNOWLEDGED\n```\n\nUse live Cable Car Drive estate.\n\nDo not touch unrelated Drive folders.\n\nTests include transient failures and duplicate polling.\n\n**Gate:** external→local delivery certified.\n\n---\n\n## SLICE 4 — RECOVERY ENGINE\n\nImplement startup reconciliation.\n\nCover all incomplete states.\n\nAdd fault injection.\n\nAcceptance requires restart at multiple checkpoints.\n\n**Gate:** restart-safe inbound certified.\n\n---\n\n## SLICE 5 — OUTBOUND RETURN\n\nBuild:\n\n```text\nlocal outbound discovery\nclaim\nupload\nhash verify\nDrive COMPLETED state\n```\n\nPreserve same `HANDOFF_ID`.\n\n**Gate:** local→external certified.\n\n---\n\n## SLICE 6 — FULL ROUND-TRIP PROVING TEST\n\nUse:\n\n```text\nCoda → Luce → Coda\n```\n\nExecute actual proving test.\n\nLuce independently verifies.\n\nNico may not self-certify.\n\n---\n\n# 25. REQUIRED TEST CLASSES\n\nMinimum automated coverage:\n\n### Contract tests\n\n- valid envelope;\n- invalid envelope;\n- filename/JSON ID mismatch;\n- unsupported schema;\n- malformed timestamp;\n- unsafe attachment name.\n\n### Identity tests\n\n- duplicate same content;\n- duplicate conflicting content;\n- filename identity preservation.\n\n### State tests\n\n- every legal transition;\n- every illegal transition;\n- retry exhaustion;\n- quarantine.\n\n### Atomicity tests\n\n- interrupted write;\n- partial payload;\n- existing destination;\n- hash mismatch.\n\n### Restart tests\n\n- restart after claim;\n- restart during copy;\n- restart after destination write;\n- restart before Drive acknowledgement;\n- restart during outbound upload.\n\n### Integration tests\n\n- Drive inbound;\n- Drive outbound;\n- missing Drive folder;\n- temporary API failure;\n- local target unavailable.\n\n### Security tests\n\n- path traversal;\n- absolute path injection;\n- executable payload remains inert;\n- oversized payload;\n- malformed ZIP where applicable.\n\n---\n\n# 26. NON-GOALS FOR V1\n\nNico must not add:\n\n- autonomous seat routing;\n- LLM interpretation;\n- prompt optimization;\n- semantic classification;\n- direct seat execution;\n- distributed message broker;\n- Redis;\n- Kafka;\n- cloud database;\n- webhook infrastructure unless required by an unavoidable Drive limitation;\n- GUI redesign;\n- Command Center redesign;\n- myDon redesign;\n- inbox-MCP redesign;\n- generalized multi-cloud transport;\n- model-provider routing.\n\nV1 should be intentionally small.\n\n---\n\n# 27. CODE SHAPE\n\nRecommended conceptual module boundaries:\n\n```text\ncable_car/\n├── config/\n├── contracts/\n│   ├── handoff\n│   ├── return\n│   └── states\n├── identity/\n│   ├── filename\n│   └── hashing\n├── state/\n│   ├── database\n│   ├── transfers\n│   └── events\n├── transport/\n│   ├── drive\n│   ├── local\n│   └── atomic\n├── workers/\n│   ├── inbound\n│   ├── outbound\n│   └── recovery\n├── security/\n│   └── validation\n├── cli/\n└── tests/\n```\n\nNico may adapt names to the existing repository conventions.\n\nHe may not collapse architectural boundaries merely for convenience.\n\n---\n\n# 28. COMMAND SURFACE\n\nMinimum useful developer commands:\n\n```text\ncable-car status\ncable-car poll-once\ncable-car run\ncable-car recover\ncable-car inspect <HANDOFF_ID>\ncable-car retry <HANDOFF_ID>\n```\n\nPotential human-only remediation command:\n\n```text\ncable-car quarantine-info <HANDOFF_ID>\n```\n\nNo destructive `force` command in initial V1 unless Don explicitly approves it.\n\n---\n\n# 29. CURRENT / HISTORICAL DISCIPLINE\n\nAll Cable Car project documentation follows the project spine:\n\n```text\nCable_Car/\n├── 00_CURRENT/\n├── 01_HANDOFFS/\n├── 02_WORK/\n├── 03_REGISTRY/\n├── 04_DECISIONS/\n└── 90_HISTORICAL/\n```\n\nWhere possible, implementation runtime artifacts stay local and Drive contains durable specifications, handoffs, registries, decisions, and appropriate transport exchange artifacts.\n\nDo not turn Google Drive into a source-code checkout.\n\n---\n\n# 30. BUILD AUTHORITY\n\n### Nico may decide:\n\n- internal function names;\n- normal class/module decomposition;\n- test utility details;\n- straightforward library choice where architecture is unaffected;\n- implementation syntax;\n- minor refactors necessary to satisfy the contract.\n\n### Nico must stop and return for architecture review if:\n\n- local canonical inbox cannot support the contract;\n- Drive state transitions cannot be represented reliably;\n- exactly-once effect requires changing routing semantics;\n- myDon must be modified materially;\n- inbox-MCP V1 must be changed materially;\n- filename identity cannot remain authoritative;\n- a security invariant cannot be implemented;\n- an architectural dependency not described here becomes necessary.\n\nNo silent architecture substitutions.\n\n---\n\n# 31. IMPLEMENTATION RETURN FORMAT\n\nAt the end of every slice Nico returns:\n\n```text\nSLICE:\nSTATUS:\nCONFIDENCE:\n\nFILES CREATED:\nFILES MODIFIED:\nFILES DELETED:\n\nARCHITECTURE CONTRACT:\n- preserved / deviation\n\nTESTS:\n- count\n- pass\n- fail\n\nINVARIANTS VERIFIED:\n\nFAULTS / RISKS:\n\nUNRESOLVED:\n\nNEXT GATE:\n\nSELF-CERTIFICATION:\nNOT PERMITTED\n```\n\n---\n\n# 32. ACCEPTANCE DEFINITION\n\nCable Car V1 is complete only when:\n\n```text\n[ ] Drive transport estate exists\n[ ] handoff schema frozen\n[ ] HANDOFF_ID invariant proven\n[ ] SQLite transfer ledger operational\n[ ] append-only event ledger operational\n[ ] atomic local delivery proven\n[ ] duplicate same-content suppressed\n[ ] duplicate changed-content quarantined\n[ ] Drive inbound operational\n[ ] Drive outbound operational\n[ ] restart recovery proven\n[ ] no Don clipboard step required\n[ ] no autonomous seat routing introduced\n[ ] myDon remains routing authority surface\n[ ] inbox-MCP V1 remains intact\n[ ] Coda→Luce→Coda proving test passes\n[ ] Luce independently verifies\n[ ] Don accepts\n```\n\nOnly after those conditions:\n\n```text\nCABLE CAR V1 = CERTIFIED\n```\n\n---\n\n# 33. NICO EXECUTION DIRECTIVE\n\n**Nico:**\n\nImplement Cable Car exactly as a transport layer.\n\nDo not optimize the architecture before proving it.\n\nDo not redesign myDon.\n\nDo not redesign the Command Center.\n\nDo not reinterpret Pigeon as an orchestration seat.\n\nDo not create a second execution queue.\n\nDo not infer authority from `requested_destination`.\n\nPreserve:\n\n```text\nCable Car = PATH\nPigeon = COURIER\nDon = ROUTING AUTHORITY\nmyDon = ROUTING SURFACE\nlocal inbox/_shared = EXECUTION INTAKE\nDrive = EXTERNAL EXCHANGE\n```\n\nBegin with **Slice 0 recon only**.\n\nReturn the recon package and implementation map before writing production Cable Car code.\n\n**PROCEED.**\n:::\n\nThis is the version I’d give Nico. The important par