ot conflict\n8. atomic rename/move into final canonical filename\n9. verify final file exists\n10. verify final hash\n11. update transfer ledger\n12. append completion event\n```\n\nIf verification fails before final commit:\n\n```text\nNO CANONICAL DESTINATION FILE\n```\n\n---\n\n# 5. DESTINATION IDENTITY\n\nFinal filename must preserve the canonical HANDOFF_ID.\n\nDo not silently rename the logical handoff.\n\nIf source envelope and canonical filename conflict, that should already have been classified by Slice 1 logic and must not reach commit.\n\nFinal local destination is conceptually:\n\n```text\n_shared\\GCE_HANDOFF_<HANDOFF_ID>.json\n```\n\nor the approved canonical filename generated by the existing parser/generator.\n\n---\n\n# 6. EXISTING DESTINATION RULES\n\nBefore commit:\n\n## Same HANDOFF_ID + same content/hash\n\nResult:\n\n```text\nDUPLICATE_SAME_CONTENT\n```\n\nBehavior:\n\n- do not overwrite;\n- do not produce second delivery;\n- record duplicate event;\n- treat exactly-once effect as preserved.\n\n## Same HANDOFF_ID + different content/hash\n\nResult:\n\n```text\nDUPLICATE_ID_CONTENT_CONFLICT\n```\n\nBehavior:\n\n- do not overwrite;\n- do not rename around conflict;\n- classify for quarantine;\n- append conflict event.\n\nNo destructive replacement in V1.\n\n---\n\n# 7. CRASH / INTERRUPTION RECOVERY\n\nSlice 2 must explicitly support interruption at these checkpoints:\n\n```text\nA. before temp write\nB. during temp write\nC. after temp write but before hash verification\nD. after hash verification but before atomic rename\nE. after atomic rename but before ledger update\nF. after ledger update but before final event append\n```\n\nOn restart, reconciliation must determine what is already true from:\n\n```text\nfilesystem\n+\ntransfer ledger\n+\nevent ledger\n+\nhashes\n```\n\nDo not assume ledger alone is authoritative if filesystem proves delivery already occurred.\n\n---\n\n# 8. ORPHAN TEMP FILES\n\nImplement reconciliation for orphan temp file