ame-content destination\n```text\nno overwrite\nno second effect\nduplicate recorded\n```\n\n### Preexisting conflicting destination\n```text\nno overwrite\nconflict classification\n```\n\n### Hash failure\n```text\nno canonical file\nerror event recorded\n```\n\n### Restart after rename / before ledger commit\nThis is critical.\n\nSimulate:\n\n```text\nfinal file exists\nledger says incomplete\n```\n\nRecovery must recognize existing matching destination and converge to delivered/acknowledged local state without rewriting the file.\n\n### Orphan temp\nTest at least:\n\n```text\npartial orphan\nvalid complete orphan\n```\n\n### Invalid destination/path\nReject traversal and foreign-path attempts.\n\n### Repeated full suite execution\nRun entire test suite twice consecutively.\n\nNo leftover test artifacts.\n\n---\n\n# 12. TEST HYGIENE\n\nNo:\n\n```text\n.skip\n.only\ntodo bypasses\narbitrary sleep-based correctness\nretry-until-green cleanup\nswallowed filesystem errors\n```\n\nIf Windows filesystem behavior requires deterministic close/dispose, implement lifecycle ownership properly.\n\n---\n\n# 13. STATE / EVENT EXPECTATION\n\nUse existing Slice 1 transfer/event infrastructure.\n\nDo not invent a second state store.\n\nMinimum local-delivery events may include:\n\n```text\nLOCAL_STAGE_STARTED\nLOCAL_STAGE_WRITTEN\nLOCAL_HASH_VERIFIED\nLOCAL_COMMIT_STARTED\nLOCAL_COMMIT_COMPLETED\nLOCAL_DUPLICATE_IGNORED\nLOCAL_CONFLICT_DETECTED\nLOCAL_RECOVERY_STARTED\nLOCAL_RECOVERY_COMPLETED\nLOCAL_HASH_MISMATCH\n```\n\nNames may vary, but semantics must be machine-readable and explicit.\n\n---\n\n# 14. OUT OF SCOPE\n\nDo NOT implement:\n\n- Google Drive watcher\n- Drive polling\n- Drive folder movement\n- Drive upload/download\n- outbound `06_OUTBOX` watcher\n- Command Center UI\n- myDon changes\n- inbox-MCP redesign\n- autonomous seat routing\n- semantic interpretation\n- LLM calls\n- Pigeon intelligence\n- webhook infrastructure\n\n---\n\n# 15. SLICE 2 RETURN CONTRACT\n\nRetu