ce 2 certification basis\n\n- **54/54 pass**\n- **two consecutive clean runs**\n- **no leftover test artifacts**\n- atomic rename proven compatible with the consumer\n- restart-after-rename convergence proven\n- duplicate same-content suppression proven\n- conflicting-content protection proven\n- hash mismatch fails closed\n- no second local queue\n- no myDon redesign\n- no inbox-MCP change\n- no Drive logic leaked into Slice 2\n\nThe SQLite FK ordering fix also makes sense: the transfer must exist before child events can reference it. That is a valid implementation correction, not an architecture deviation.\n\nSo the gate is:\n\n```text\nSLICE 0: ACCEPTED\nSLICE 1: CERTIFIED\nSLICE 2: CERTIFIED\nSLICE 3: AUTHORIZED\n```\n\n## Next scope: Slice 3 — Drive inbound adapter\n\nNico can now implement only this path:\n\n```text\nGoogle Drive / 01_INBOUND_TO_GCE\n→ discover\n→ validate\n→ claim\n→ move to 03_IN_FLIGHT\n→ download\n→ invoke existing localDelivery\n→ verify local ACKNOWLEDGED\n→ move Drive item to 04_ACKNOWLEDGED\n```\n\nThe key rule for Slice 3 is: **do not duplicate any of the local delivery logic**. The Drive adapter should terminate into the already-certified `localDelivery` module.\n\nAnd because the Drive folder IDs now exist in our actual GCE estate, Slice 3 should use those IDs in config rather than runtime folder-name discovery wherever possible.\n\nIf you want, I’ll give you the exact Slice 3 Nico prompt next.", "text_chars": 1772, "code_blocks": 3, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "4260abef-b82b-4500-8e30-1f039583af05", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790286143.685, "updated_at": 1790286212.031347, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "yes", "text_chars": 3, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "3ffcde98-bd7d-450a-9343-17d8c4f5bba4", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790286148.581835, "updated_at": 1790286358.525285, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Absolutely. Send Nico this:\n\n:::writing{variant=\"document\" id=\"86241\" title=\"Cable Car Slice 3 — Drive Inbound Adapter Build Prompt\"}\n# GCE CABLE CAR — SLICE 3 IMPLEMENTATION DIRECTIVE\n\n**Authority:** Don  \n**Architecture / Methodology:** Coda  \n**Implementation Seat:** Nico  \n**Verification Seat:** Luce  \n**Status:** AUTHORIZED  \n**Prior Gates:** Slice 1 CERTIFIED, Slice 2 CERTIFIED  \n**Scope:** GOOGLE DRIVE INBOUND ADAPTER ONLY  \n**Do Not Advance To:** outbound return path\n\n---\n\n## OBJECTIVE\n\nImplement the inbound transport path:\n\n```text\nGoogle Drive / 01_INBOUND_TO_GCE\n→ discover\n→ validate\n→ claim\n→ move to 03_IN_FLIGHT\n→ download\n→ invoke certified localDelivery\n→ confirm local ACKNOWLEDGED\n→ move Drive artifact to 04_ACKNOWLEDGED\n```\n\nThis slice must reuse the already-certified local delivery path.\n\nDo not reimplement atomic local delivery inside the Drive adapter.\n\n---\n\n# 1. ARCHITECTURE BOUNDARY\n\nPreserve:\n\n```text\nDrive = transport state\nCable Car adapter = transport bridge\nlocalDelivery = local atomic commit authority\n_shared = canonical execution intake\ninbox-mcp = existing consumer\nmyDon = routing surface\nDon = routing authority\n```\n\nThe Drive adapter owns only:\n\n```text\nDrive discovery\nDrive validation\nDrive claim/state transition\nDrive download\nhandoff into localDelivery\nDrive acknowledgement state\nDrive-side retry/error handling\n```\n\nIt does not own:\n\n```text\nlocal atomic write logic\nseat routing\nprompt interpretation\nexecution\nverification judgment\noutbound return\n```\n\n---\n\n# 2. DRIVE ESTATE\n\nCanonical project home:\n\n```text\nGCE/\n└── 03_PROJECTS/\n    └── GCE_Stack/\n        └── Transport/\n            └── Cable_Car/\n```\n\nRuntime transport folders:\n\n```text\n01_INBOUND_TO_GCE\n03_IN_FLIGHT\n04_ACKNOWLEDGED\n90_FAILED\n98_QUARANTINE\n```\n\nSlice 3 does not need:\n\n```text\n02_OUTBOUND_FROM_GCE\n05_COMPLETED\n```\n\nexcept as known future config entries.\n\n---\n\n# 3. FOLDER ID RULE\n\nUse Drive folder IDs in config.\n\nDo not rely on repeated runtime folder-name search once IDs are known.\n\nConfig should expose logical keys such as:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"drive\": {\n    \"inboundFolderId\": \"...\",\n    \"inFlightFolderId\": \"...\",\n    \"acknowledgedFolderId\": \"...\",\n    \"failedFolderId\": \"...\",\n    \"quarantineFolderId\": \"...\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\nBootstrap/discovery tooling may resolve IDs once.\n\nNormal runtime uses IDs.\n\n---\n\n# 4. DRIVE ADAPTER MODULE\n\nRecommended boundary:\n\n```text\ntransport/driveInbound.js\n```\n\nor equivalent.\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n- list inbound candidates;\n- map Drive metadata into transport candidate;\n- validate supported artifact type;\n- claim candidate;\n- move candidate into `03_IN_FLIGHT`;\n- download bytes;\n- calculate/verify Drive-side hash where possible;\n- invoke `localDelivery.deliver(...)`;\n- inspect result;\n- move Drive candidate to `04_ACKNOWLEDGED`;\n- emit transfer events.\n\nKeep Drive API mechanics isolated from localDelivery.\n\n---\n\n# 5. DISCOVERY RULES\n\nOnly inspect direct children of:\n\n```text\n01_INBOUND_TO_GCE\n```\n\nfor Slice 3.\n\nDo not recursively crawl unrelated Drive folders.\n\nSupported V1 inbound artifact:\n\n```text\nGCE_HANDOFF_<HANDOFF_ID>.json\n```\n\nOptional future attachments are out of scope unless already required by the current contract.\n\nIgnore unsupported non-handoff files or quarantine them according to explicit contract behavior.\n\nDo not silently process arbitrary Drive content.\n\n---\n\n# 6. CLAIMING RULE\n\nBefore downloading:\n\n```text\ncheck local ledger\n→ validate identity\n→ establish claim\n→ move Drive artifact INBOUND → IN_FLIGHT\n→ confirm Drive parent/state\n```\n\nThe Drive move is part of the durable claim.\n\nIf the move fails:\n\n```text\ndo not continue to local delivery\n```\n\nIf the artifact is no longer in inbound after discovery:\n\n```text\nreconcile\ndo not assume ownership\n```\n\nTwo workers observing the same file must not both deliver it.\n\nExactly-once effect remains:\n\n```text\nat-least-once observation\n+\ndurable claim\n+\nidempotent localDelivery\n=\nexactly-once local effect\n```\n\n---\n\n# 7. VALIDATION BEFORE CLAIM\n\nValidate at minimum:\n\n- filename contract;\n- HANDOFF_ID;\n- supported extension;\n- MIME/type expectations;\n- schema version after download;\n- filename ID vs envelope ID;\n- maximum configured size.\n\nUnsafe or malformed artifact:\n\n```text\n→ 98_QUARANTINE\n```\n\nDo not route malformed input into `_shared`.\n\n---\n\n# 8. DOWNLOAD CONTRACT\n\nDownload into Cable Car-owned staging/runtime memory/path.\n\nDo not download directly into `_shared`.\n\nSequence:\n\n```text\nDrive download\n→ Cable Car staging\n→ hash\n→ envelope validation\n→ localDelivery\n```\n\nOnce `localDelivery` receives the artifact, Slice 2 rules control local commit.\n\n---\n\n# 9. LOCAL DELIVERY INTEGRATION\n\nThe adapter must call the existing certified implementation.\n\nConceptually:\n\n```js\nawait localDelivery.deliver(candidate)\n```\n\nDo not copy/paste its logic.\n\nThe Drive adapter must consume explicit localDelivery outcomes, including:\n\n```text\nACKNOWLEDGED\nDUPLICATE_SAME_CONTENT\nDUPLICATE_ID_CONTENT_CONFLICT\nHASH_MISMATCH\nQUARANTINED / ERROR\n```\n\nDrive-side state must respond deterministically to each.\n\n---\n\n# 10. ACKNOWLEDGEMENT RULE\n\nOnly move Drive artifact:\n\n```text\n03_IN_FLIGHT\n→ 04_ACKNOWLEDGED\n```\n\nafter local state proves:\n\n```text\ncanonical _shared file exists\nAND\nfinal hash matches\nAND\ntransfer ledger says ACKNOWLEDGED\n```\n\nDo not treat “download succeeded” as acknowledgement.\n\nDo not treat “localDelivery started” as acknowledgement.\n\n---\n\n# 11. DUPLICATE BEHAVIOR\n\n## Same HANDOFF_ID + same hash, already ACKNOWLEDGED locally\n\nIf rediscovered:\n\n```text\nNO SECOND LOCAL DELIVERY\n```\n\nReconcile Drive state into:\n\n```text\n04_ACKNOWLEDGED\n```\n\nand append duplicate/reconciliation event.\n\n## Same HANDOFF_ID + different hash\n\n```text\n98_QUARANTINE\n```\n\nDo not overwrite.\n\nDo not rename around identity conflict.\n\n---\n\n# 12. RETRY POLICY\n\nUse existing approved defaults:\n\n```text\npoll interval: 15 sec\n\nretry:\n5 sec\n15 sec\n60 sec\n300 sec\n900 sec\n\nmax attempts: 5\n```\n\nRetry only transient failures, e.g.:\n\n- temporary Drive API error;\n- download interruption;\n- temporary network error;\n- transient move failure.\n\nDo not retry deterministic validation failures.\n\nAfter retry exhaustion:\n\n```text\n90_FAILED\n```\n\n---\n\n# 13. FAILURE CLASSIFICATION\n\n## QUARANTINE\n\nExamples:\n\n```text\nfilename invalid\nschema invalid\nID mismatch\nunsupported schema version\noversized payload\nduplicate ID / changed content\nunsafe metadata\n```\n\n## RETRYABLE\n\nExamples:\n\n```text\nDrive 5xx\nnetwork interruption\ntemporary read failure\ntemporary folder move failure\n```\n\n## FATAL CONFIG\n\nExamples:\n\n```text\nmissing folder IDs\nunreachable configured Drive root\ninvalid local shared path\nstate DB unavailable\n```\n\nFail closed.\n\n---\n\n# 14. EVENT MODEL\n\nAdd Drive-specific events, e.g.:\n\n```text\nDRIVE_DISCOVERED\nDRIVE_VALIDATION_STARTED\nDRIVE_VALIDATION_PASSED\nDRIVE_CLAIM_STARTED\nDRIVE_CLAIMED\nDRIVE_DOWNLOAD_STARTED\nDRIVE_DOWNLOAD_COMPLETED\nDRIVE_LOCAL_DELIVERY_STARTED\nDRIVE_LOCAL_DELIVERY_ACKNOWLEDGED\nDRIVE_ACK_MOVE_STARTED\nDRIVE_ACKNOWLEDGED\nDRIVE_RETRY_SCHEDULED\nDRIVE_QUARANTINED\nDRIVE_FAILED\nDRIVE_RECONCILED\n```\n\nNames may vary, but transitions must be machine-readable.\n\n---\n\n# 15. RECOVERY / RECONCILIATION\n\nSlice 3 must support restart during:\n\n```text\nA. after discovery, before claim\nB. after move to IN_FLIGHT, before download\nC. during download\nD. after download, before localDelivery\nE. after localDelivery ACKNOWLEDGED, before Drive ack move\nF. after Drive ack move, before final event append\n```\n\nOn startup/recovery inspect:\n\n```text\nDrive parent/state\n+\nlocal transfer ledger\n+\nlocal destination file\n+\nhashes\n```\n\nRequired convergence examples:\n\n### Case A\n\nDrive = IN_FLIGHT  \nLocal destination absent\n\n```text\nresume download/delivery\n```\n\n### Case B\n\nDrive = IN_FLIGHT  \nLocal ledger = ACKNOWLEDGED  \nDestination hash matches\n\n```text\nmove Drive → ACKNOWLEDGED\n```\n\n### Case C\n\nDrive = INBOUND  \nLocal ledger = ACKNOWLEDGED  \nDestination hash matches\n\n```text\ndo not redeliver\nreconcile Drive → ACKNOWLEDGED\n```\n\n### Case D\n\nDrive = IN_FLIGHT  \nLocal destination conflicting\n\n```text\nquarantine\ndo not overwrite\n```\n\n---\n\n# 16. POLL-ONCE FIRST\n\nBefore a long-running watcher, implement and certify:\n\n```text\ncable-car poll-once\n```\n\nIt should:\n\n```text\ninspect current inbound\nprocess bounded candidate set\nreconcile\nexit cleanly\n```\n\nThis gives deterministic testability.\n\nLong-running:\n\n```text\ncable-car run\n```\n\nmay wrap `poll-once` later.\n\nDo not make daemon behavior the only way to test the adapter.\n\n---\n\n# 17. REQUIRED TESTS\n\nMinimum new test coverage:\n\n## Discovery\n- inbound valid candidate discovered\n- unrelated file ignored/quarantined as contract states\n- only configured inbound folder inspected\n\n## Claim\n- successful INBOUND → IN_FLIGHT\n- claim move failure causes no delivery\n- two-worker/double-claim simulation does not double-deliver\n\n## Download\n- successful download\n- transient download failure retries\n- malformed downloaded payload quarantined\n\n## Integration with localDelivery\n-