fers.create(...)\n```\n\nthen the Drive adapter will collide with the unique `handoff_id`.\n\nDo NOT work around this by creating duplicate IDs or deleting the transfer.\n\nInstead make the API explicitly support:\n\n```text\nexisting transfer → continue delivery\n```\n\nwhile preserving standalone Slice 2 behavior.\n\nAcceptable pattern:\n\n```text\nfind transfer\nif absent → create\nif present and compatible → reuse\nif present and conflicting → deterministic conflict\n```\n\nAdd a regression test for this exact integration path.\n\n---\n\n## 7. LOCAL DELIVERY RESULT HANDLING\n\nHandle explicit outcomes.\n\n### ACKNOWLEDGED\n\n```text\nmove Drive IN_FLIGHT → ACKNOWLEDGED\n```\n\n### DUPLICATE_SAME_CONTENT\n\nIf local canonical destination is verified:\n\n```text\nreconcile Drive → ACKNOWLEDGED\n```\n\nNo second local write.\n\n### DUPLICATE_ID_CONTENT_CONFLICT\n\n```text\nDrive → QUARANTINE\n```\n\n### HASH_MISMATCH / deterministic validation failure\n\n```text\nDrive → QUARANTINE\n```\n\n### retryable local filesystem failure\n\nDo not mark Drive acknowledged.\n\nPreserve/retry from IN_FLIGHT.\n\n---\n\n## 8. QUARANTINE HELPERS\n\n`_quarantine()` and `_quarantineById()` must not suppress move failures.\n\nRequired sequence:\n\n```text\nrecord intent\nattempt Drive move\nverify success\nupdate transfer state = QUARANTINED\nappend successful quarantine event\n```\n\nIf the move fails:\n\n```text\nrecord quarantine-move failure\nthrow\n```\n\nDo not leave ledger claiming QUARANTINED while the file physically remains elsewhere without recording the inconsistency.\n\n---\n\n## 9. DRIVE / LOCAL STATE ORDERING\n\nMaintain this invariant:\n\n```text\nphysical state and ledger state must converge\n```\n\nDo not append a final state event before the physical Drive move that establishes that state has succeeded.\n\nExamples:\n\nCorrect:\n\n```text\nDRIVE_ACK_MOVE_STARTED\n→ moveFile()\n→ transfer/state reconciliation\n→ DRIVE_ACKNOWLEDGED\n```\n\nIncorrect:\n\n```text\nmark