s now:\n\n```text\nSLICE 0: ACCEPTED\nSLICE 1: CERTIFIED\nSLICE 2: CERTIFIED\nSLICE 3: CERTIFIED\n```\n\n## Next step\n\nThe next architecture slice should be **Slice 4 — Recovery Engine / Restart Reconciliation Hardening**.\n\nNot outbound yet.\n\nWhy: we have proven the happy path and quarantine path live, but before adding the reverse leg we should harden the incomplete-state recovery cases so Cable Car can survive interruption anywhere between:\n\n```text\nINBOUND\n→ IN_FLIGHT\n→ local delivery\n→ Drive ACK\n```\n\nSlice 4 should prove deterministic recovery for cases like:\n\n```text\nDrive = IN_FLIGHT\nlocal file absent\n→ resume delivery\n\nDrive = IN_FLIGHT\nlocal file present + matching hash\nledger incomplete\n→ reconcile to ACK\n\nDrive = INBOUND\nledger already ACKNOWLEDGED\n→ no redelivery, reconcile Drive\n\nDrive = IN_FLIGHT\nlocal conflicting file\n→ quarantine\n\nphysical Drive move succeeded\nfinal ledger event missing\n→ reconcile event/state only\n```\n\n### One ruling before we continue\n\nDo **not** have Nico archive or rewrite evidence/history yet.\n\nKeep the evidence files where they are for now. We’ll finish Slice 4 and then make one deliberate documentation/archive pass rather than sprinkling historical artifacts throughout the build.\n\nIf you want, I’ll give you the **Slice 4 Nico build prompt** next.", "text_chars": 2184, "code_blocks": 4, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "13245324-ecd4-45a9-8327-62204a165ad6", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790302716.488, "updated_at": 1790302775.123577, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "yes", "text_chars": 3, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "a74d4997-7c02-4c7f-8f6e-5e486f3f0a41", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790302722.636117, "updated_at": 1790307956.087848, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Absolutely. Send Nico this next.\n\n:::writing{variant=\"document\" title=\"Cable Car Slice 4 — Recovery Engine / Restart Reconciliation Hardening\"}\n# GCE CABLE CAR — SLICE 4 IMPLEMENTATION DIRECTIVE\n\n**Authority:** Don  \n**Architecture / Methodology:** Coda  \n**Implementation Seat:** Nico  \n**Verification Seat:** Luce  \n**Status:** AUTHORIZED  \n**Prior Gates:** Slice 1 CERTIFIED · Slice 2 CERTIFIED · Slice 3 CERTIFIED  \n**Scope:** RECOVERY ENGINE / RESTART RECONCILIATION HARDENING  \n**Do Not Advance To:** outbound return transport\n\n---\n\n## OBJECTIVE\n\nBuild the deterministic recovery layer for incomplete inbound transport state.\n\nSlice 3 proved the live path:\n\n```text\nDrive inbound\n→ claim\n→ download\n→ localDelivery\n→ local ACK\n→ Drive ACK\n```\n\nSlice 4 must prove Cable Car can restart at any intermediate point and converge safely without:\n\n- duplicate local delivery;\n- overwriting conflicting content;\n- losing a valid in-flight handoff;\n- inventing state;\n- silently promoting quarantined transfers;\n- depending on manual cleanup.\n\nCanonical recovery inputs:\n\n```text\nDrive parent/state\n+\nlocal transfer ledger\n+\nevent ledger\n+\ncanonical local destination\n+\nstaging/temp state\n+\nhashes\n```\n\nRecovery must reconcile these sources into one correct terminal or resumable state.\n\n---\n\n# 1. ARCHITECTURE BOUNDARY\n\nPreserve:\n\n```text\nDrive = transport state\nSQLite = durable transport ledger\nfilesystem = physical delivery truth\nlocalDelivery = atomic local commit authority\n_shared = canonical local execution intake\nrecovery = reconciliation engine\n```\n\nRecovery may:\n\n- inspect;\n- compare;\n- verify;\n- resume;\n- reconcile;\n- append events;\n- complete an interrupted transition.\n\nRecovery may NOT:\n\n- reinterpret handoff content;\n- change routing;\n- clear quarantine without explicit authority;\n- mutate identity;\n- replace conflicting canonical files;\n- fabricate missing payload content;\n- reset history.\n\n---\n\n# 2. MODULE BOUNDARY\n\nRecommended module:\n\n```text\nworkers/recovery.js\n```\n\nor equivalent.\n\nDo not bury recovery logic inside `driveInbound.js`.\n\nThe inbound adapter may call the recovery engine, but recovery should be independently testable.\n\n---\n\n# 3. REQUIRED RECOVERY COMMAND\n\nImplement:\n\n```text\ncable-car recover\n```\n\nand preferably a bounded internal API such as:\n\n```js\nawait recovery.reconcileAll()\n```\n\nRecovery must be safe to run repeatedly.\n\nIdempotent expectation:\n\n```text\nrecover\n→ recover\n→ recover\n```\n\nmust produce the same final state after convergence.\n\n---\n\n# 4. RECOVERY MATRIX\n\nImplement explicit handling for at least these cases.\n\n## CASE A — Drive IN_FLIGHT, local destination absent\n\nState:\n\n```text\nDrive = IN_FLIGHT\nledger = IN_FLIGHT / RETRYABLE_FAILURE / incomplete\ncanonical local file = absent\n```\n\nAction:\n\n```text\nresume download\n→ validate\n→ localDelivery\n→ ACK\n```\n\nDo not create a second transfer row.\n\n---\n\n## CASE B — Drive IN_FLIGHT, local file exists and hash matches\n\nState:\n\n```text\nDrive = IN_FLIGHT\ncanonical local file = present\nhash = expected\nledger incomplete\n```\n\nAction:\n\n```text\ndo not rewrite\nreconcile ledger to ACKNOWLEDGED\nmove Drive → ACKNOWLEDGED\nappend recovery events\n```\n\nThis is one of the most important Slice 4 cases.\n\n---\n\n## CASE C — Drive INBOUND, local ledger already ACKNOWLEDGED\n\nState:\n\n```text\nDrive = INBOUND\nledger = ACKNOWLEDGED\ncanonical file = present\nhash matches\n```\n\nAction:\n\n```text\ndo not redeliver\nmove Drive → ACKNOWLEDGED\nappend reconciliation event\n```\n\nExactly-once effect must remain intact.\n\n---\n\n## CASE D — Drive IN_FLIGHT, canonical local file conflicts\n\nState:\n\n```text\nDrive = IN_FLIGHT\ncanonical file = present\nhash != expected\n```\n\nAction:\n\n```text\nDO NOT overwrite\nDO NOT rename around conflict\nDrive → QUARANTINE\nledger → QUARANTINED\nappend conflict/recovery events\n```\n\n---\n\n## CASE E — Drive move succeeded, final event missing\n\nExample:\n\n```text\nDrive = ACKNOWLEDGED\nledger = ACKNOWLEDGED\nevent history missing DRIVE_ACKNOWLEDGED\n```\n\nAction:\n\n```text\nappend missing reconciliation/final event\ndo not move file again\ndo not redeliver\n```\n\nPhysical state wins over replaying the transport effect.\n\n---\n\n## CASE F — local file exists, ledger missing\n\nState:\n\n```text\ncanonical local file = present\nledger row = absent\nDrive = IN_FLIGHT or ACKNOWLEDGED\n```\n\nAction must be conservative.\n\nRequired:\n\n```text\nderive HANDOFF_ID\nverify filename\nhash local file\ninspect Drive artifact\ncompare hashes\n```\n\nIf identity + hash prove this is the same transfer:\n\n```text\nreconstruct ledger deterministically\nappend RECOVERY_RECONSTRUCTED event\n```\n\nIf proof is insufficient:\n\n```text\nSTOP / QUARANTINE\n```\n\nDo not invent provenance.\n\n---\n\n## CASE G — orphan staging temp\n\nState:\n\n```text\ntemp exists\ncanonical file absent\nledger incomplete or absent\n```\n\nRequired classification:\n\n- partial/unverified temp → safe cleanup or quarantine\n- complete valid temp + matching transfer → resume\n- temp with no trustworthy transfer identity → quarantine or retain for manual review\n\nDo not blindly promote temp files.\n\n---\n\n## CASE H — quarantined transfer reappears inbound\n\nState:\n\n```text\nledger = QUARANTINED\nsame HANDOFF_ID reappears\n```\n\nRequired:\n\n```text\ndo not reprocess\ndo not promote\nreconcile to quarantine\n```\n\nThis preserves the LIVE_001 ruling.\n\n---\n\n## CASE I — Drive ACKNOWLEDGED but local canonical file missing\n\nThis is a serious inconsistency.\n\nRequired behavior:\n\n```text\ndo not silently declare success\nappend RECOVERY_INCONSISTENCY\nfail closed / escalate\n```\n\nIf the source Drive artifact is still retrievable and policy permits deterministic restoration, return evidence before implementing automatic restoration.\n\nDo not make that architectural decision yourself.\n\n---\n\n# 5. STATE PRECEDENCE\n\nRecovery must reason from evidence, not one source alone.\n\nRecommended precedence for transport reconciliation:\n\n```text\ncontent hash + physical file existence\n> physical Drive parent/state\n> durable transfer row\n> event history\n> transient process memory\n```\n\nBut no single source may override a proven conflict.\n\nExample:\n\n```text\nledger says ACKNOWLEDGED\nbut local canonical file hash conflicts\n```\n\nResult:\n\n```text\nINCONSISTENCY / QUARANTINE\n```\n\nnot “trust ledger.”\n\n---\n\n# 6. RECOVERY EVENTS\n\nAdd explicit recovery telemetry, e.g.:\n\n```text\nRECOVERY_STARTED\nRECOVERY_INSPECTED\nRECOVERY_RESUME_DOWNLOAD\nRECOVERY_LOCAL_ALREADY_PRESENT\nRECOVERY_LEDGER_RECONSTRUCTED\nRECOVERY_DRIVE_RECONCILED\nRECOVERY_EVENT_REPAIRED\nRECOVERY_CONFLICT\nRECOVERY_ORPHAN_TEMP\nRECOVERY_INCONSISTENCY\nRECOVERY_COMPLETED\n```\n\nExact names may vary.\n\nSemantics must be clear and machine-readable.\n\n---\n\n# 7. NO HISTORY REWRITES\n\nEvent history remains append-only.\n\nRecovery may append corrective/reconciliation events.\n\nRecovery may not:\n\n- rewrite old events;\n- delete old events;\n- change prior timestamps;\n- “fix” history in place.\n\nCanonical method:\n\n```text\nold state remains\n+\nnew reconciliation event explains convergence\n```\n\n---\n\n# 8. RETRY INTERACTION\n\nRecovery must distinguish:\n\n```text\nretryable incomplete state\nvs\ndeterministic conflict\nvs\nterminal quarantine\n```\n\nDo not turn quarantine into retry.\n\nDo not turn deterministic hash conflict into retry.\n\nDo not restart exhausted failures without explicit policy.\n\n---\n\n# 9. CLI BEHAVIOR\n\nImplement:\n\n```text\nnode cli/index.js recover\n```\n\nRecommended output:\n\n```text\nRecovery scan\n-------------\nTransfers inspected: N\nRecovered: N\nAlready consistent: N\nQuarantined: N\nInconsistencies: N\nErrors: N\n```\n\nNo destructive auto-fix without a classified recovery rule.\n\n---\n\n# 10. REQUIRED UNIT / INTEGRATION TESTS\n\nAt minimum:\n\n### Case A\nDrive IN_FLIGHT + no local file → resumes and ACKs.\n\n### Case B\nDrive IN_FLIGHT + matching local file → no rewrite, ACK reconciliation.\n\n### Case C\nDrive INBOUND + local ACK → no redelivery, Drive reconciles.\n\n### Case D\nDrive IN_FLIGHT + conflicting local file → quarantine.\n\n### Case E\nDrive ACK + missing final event → event repaired only.\n\n### Case F\nlocal file + no ledger + provable matching Drive artifact → deterministic reconstruction.\n\n### Case F-negative\nlocal file + no ledger + insufficient proof → fail closed.\n\n### Case G\norphan partial temp → no promotion.\n\n### Case G-valid\nvalid complete temp + compatible transfer → resume.\n\n### Case H\nQUARANTINED HANDOFF_ID reappears → no reprocessing.\n\n### Case I\nDrive ACK + local file missing → inconsistency surfaced.\n\n### Repeated recovery\nRun `recover` twice against same converged state → second pass no-op.\n\n---\n\n# 11. FAULT-INJECTION TESTS\n\nSimulate crashes at:\n\n```text\nafter Drive claim\nafter download\nafter local temp write\nafter atomic rename\nafter ledger ACK\nafter Drive move to ACK\nbefore final event append\n```\n\nEach restart must converge safely.\n\nNo duplicate canonical file.\n\nNo duplicate transfer row.\n\nNo duplicate Drive artifact.\n\n---\n\n# 12. LIVE RECOVERY PROOF\n\nAfter mock/integration coverage is green, perform one controlled live recovery proof in the real Cable Car Drive estate.\n\nPreferred live scenario:\n\n```text\nDrive file = IN_FLIGHT\nlocal delivery already present and hash-matching\nledger deliberately left incomplete by controlled faul