t Don answer:\n\n> “What do we actually have right now, what really works, what is still missing, and what parts of the prior process were just loop scaffolding?”\n\n---\n\n# SWARM / SUB-AGENT LANES\n\nLaunch multiple bounded sub-agents.\n\nMinimum lanes:\n\n## AGENT 1 — LOCAL CODE / IMPLEMENTATION TRUTH\n\nInspect:\n\n```text\nC:\\Users\\Dekan AI Brother\\GCE_DON\\command-center\\cable-car\\\n```\n\nDetermine:\n\n- actual module structure\n- files created/modified\n- what each module really does\n- which slices have real code behind them\n- whether inbound path exists\n- whether recovery exists\n- whether outbound exists\n- whether OAuth support exists\n- whether any claimed feature is missing from code\n\nReturn only evidence-backed findings.\n\n---\n\n## AGENT 2 — TEST / REGRESSION TRUTH\n\nInspect all Cable Car test files and runner configuration.\n\nDetermine:\n\n- total current test count\n- which behaviors are actually covered\n- whether prior claims such as 44/44, 54/54, 69/69, 89/89 are consistent with current suite evolution\n- whether any `.skip`, `.only`, TODO, or bypass exists\n- whether tests use mocks vs real Drive\n- whether any test result was mischaracterized as live proof\n\nClassify each major capability:\n\n```text\nUNIT TESTED\nINTEGRATION TESTED\nFAULT-INJECTION TESTED\nLIVE PROVEN\nNOT PROVEN\n```\n\n---\n\n## AGENT 3 — SQLITE / STATE / EVENT TRUTH\n\nInspect the production and test state implementation read-only.\n\nDetermine:\n\n- schema\n- transfer states\n- event model\n- actual production ledger entries\n- LIVE_001 state\n- LIVE_002 state\n- Slice 4 live recovery state\n- whether historical claims match actual rows/events\n- whether any inconsistent or orphaned state exists\n\nDo not mutate the database.\n\nReturn exact current ledger truth.\n\n---\n\n## AGENT 4 — GOOGLE DRIVE / TRANSPORT TRUTH\n\nRead-only inspect the actual Cable Car Drive estate:\n\n```text\nGCE/\n03_PROJECTS/\nGCE_Stack/\nTransport/\nCable_Car/\n```\n\nDetermine actual contents/state of:\n\n```text\n01_INBOUND_TO_GCE\n02_OUTBOUND_FROM_GCE\n03_IN_FLIGHT\n04_ACKNOWLEDGED\n05_COMPLETED\n90_FAILED\n98_QUARANTINE\n99_ARCHIVE\n```\n\nVerify:\n\n- LIVE_001 location\n- LIVE_002 location\n- Slice 4 live fixture location/state\n- whether outbound/completed contains any real return artifact\n- whether Drive state matches ledger claims\n\nDo not move or create anything.\n\n---\n\n## AGENT 5 — AUTH / CONFIG / CAPABILITY TRUTH\n\nInspect read-only:\n\n- `.env`\n- `.env.example`\n- auth client implementation\n- service-account support\n- OAuth support\n- current config loader\n- current Drive mode handling\n- secrets paths by reference only, not contents\n- whether outbound write is actually possible with current configured identity\n- whether OAuth bootstrap was completed or only started\n\nDo not expose secret material.\n\nDetermine:\n\n```text\nAUTH IMPLEMENTED\nAUTH CONFIGURED\nAUTH LIVE-PROVEN\nAUTH BLOCKED\n```\n\nfor both inbound and outbound.\n\n---\n\n## AGENT 6 — HANDOFF / OPERATIONAL TRUTH\n\nInspect:\n\n- `CABLE_CAR_RECON.md`\n- live fixture files\n- evidence package files\n- any temp evidence still referenced\n- outbox path\n- `_shared`\n- inbox-MCP assumptions\n\nDetermine:\n\n- exact current canonical inbound local path\n- exact current outbound local path\n- whether outbound path semantics are actually established\n- whether manual Don file movement is still required anywhere\n- what visible operational workflow currently exists\n\n---\n\n## AGENT 7 — LOOP / PROCESS CONTAMINATION\n\nUsing the actual project artifacts plus session history available in context, classify what was:\n\n```text\nIMPLEMENTATION NECESSITY\nVALID VERIFICATION\nDUPLICATED PROCESS\nUNNECESSARY GATE\nUNNECESSARY SLICE\nCoda/Luce/Nico boundary drift\n```\n\nDo not judge models.\n\nFocus on orchestration/process.\n\nIdentify process artifacts that should NOT be treated as technical canon.\n\n---\n\n# SHARED TODO\n\nMaintain one explicit shared TODO list like:\n\n```text\n[ ] establish code truth\n[ ] establish test truth\n[ ] establish ledger truth\n[ ] establish Drive truth\n[ ] establish auth truth\n[ ] establish operational truth\n[ ] reconcile contradictions\n[ ] produce final truth matrix\n[ ] produce salvage map\n[ ] identify exact remaining gap to full round trip\n```\n\nDo not create a new TODO list per sub-agent that loses global state.\n\n---\n\n# RECONCILIATION RULE\n\nWhen sub-agents disagree:\n\n```text\nactual code / filesystem / Drive / DB evidence\n> test evidence\n> logs\n> written handoffs\n> prompts\n> memory / inference\n```\n\nIf truth cannot be determined:\n\n```text\nUNKNOWN\n```\n\nDo not fill gaps.\n\n---\n\n# REQUIRED FINAL OUTPUT\n\nProduce one consolidated report with these sections:\n\n## A. CURRENT SYSTEM TRUTH\n\nOne table:\n\n| Capability | Status | Evidence | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n\nMinimum rows:\n\n- local state engine\n- idempotency\n- atomic local delivery\n- inbound Drive adapter\n- real Drive auth\n- quarantine\n- restart durability\n- recovery engine\n- outbound source path\n- outbound adapter\n- outbound upload auth\n- return envelope transport\n- full round trip\n\nStatus values only:\n\n```text\nBUILT\nTESTED\nLIVE-PROVEN\nPARTIAL\nBLOCKED\nNOT BUILT\nUNKNOWN\n```\n\n---\n\n## B. ACTUAL FILE / MODULE MAP\n\nList only real files/modules that currently exist and matter.\n\nFor each:\n\n- path\n- purpose\n- current state\n- whether production or test-only\n\n---\n\n## C. TEST TRUTH\n\nReport:\n\n- current total test count\n- suite breakdown\n- mock vs real\n- fault injection coverage\n- skipped/bypassed tests if any\n- what is not covered\n\n---\n\n## D. LIVE EVIDENCE TRUTH\n\nReconstruct:\n\n### LIVE_001\n- what was dropped\n- what happened\n- current Drive state\n- current ledger state\n- what it proves\n\n### LIVE_002\nsame fields\n\n### SLICE4 LIVE\nsame fields\n\nDo not treat prior prose as proof if actual state disagrees.\n\n---\n\n## E. DRIVE TRUTH\n\nReturn exact current folder-state summary.\n\nNo speculative “should be.”\n\n---\n\n## F. AUTH TRUTH\n\nSeparate:\n\n```text\nSERVICE ACCOUNT INBOUND\nUSER OAUTH OUTBOUND\n```\n\nFor each:\n\n- implemented\n- configured\n- authenticated\n- capability proven\n- blocker\n\n---\n\n## G. WHAT IS ACTUALLY RUNNABLE BY DON TODAY\n\nAnswer plainly:\n\n> “What can Don do right now with Cable Car without developer intervention?”\n\nBe concrete.\n\n---\n\n## H. WHAT IS STILL MISSING\n\nOnly real missing capabilities.\n\nDo not invent future architecture.\n\n---\n\n## I. LOOP ARTIFACTS / PROCESS DEBRIS\n\nList prompts, gates, slice labels, certification wrappers, or duplicate process artifacts that should not be mistaken for technical state.\n\n---\n\n## J. SALVAGE MAP\n\nClassify:\n\n```text\nKEEP\nVERIFY\nDISCARD\nUNKNOWN\n```\n\nfor:\n\n- code\n- tests\n- docs\n- Drive artifacts\n- DB state\n- evidence files\n- process scaffolding\n\n---\n\n## K. CONTRADICTIONS FOUND\n\nFor every contradiction:\n\n```text\nCLAIM:\nEVIDENCE:\nRULING:\n```\n\nExamples to explicitly check:\n\n- outbound path claimed vs actual\n- OAuth claimed vs actual\n- service-account write capability\n- LIVE fixture paths\n- archive/history mutation\n- slice certification vs independent verification\n\n---\n\n## L. SINGLE SENTENCE CURRENT STATE\n\nEnd with one sentence:\n\n> “Cable Car currently is __________.”\n\nNo roadmap.\n\nNo new build plan.\n\n---\n\n# SESSION FOOTER\n\nEnd the report with:\n\n```text\nGCE RECON FOOTER\n\nMODE:\nREAD-ONLY\n\nFILES MODIFIED:\nNONE\n\nDRIVE MODIFIED:\nNONE\n\nDB MODIFIED:\nNONE\n\nSUB-AGENTS USED:\n[list]\n\nCONTRADICTIONS:\n[count]\n\nUNKNOWN ITEMS:\n[count]\n\nCURRENT TRUTH CONFIDENCE:\n[%]\n\nBUILD CONTINUED:\nNO\n\nCERTIFICATION ISSUED:\nNO\n\nNEXT ACTION:\nRETURN TO DON + CODA FOR REVIEW\n```\n\n---\n\n# EXECUTION DIRECTIVE\n\nUse the swarm.\n\nParallelize the recon aggressively.\n\nDo not let one agent become the narrator for all lanes.\n\nReconcile only after each lane returns