ngs it into GCE\n→ GCE works it\n→ Cable Car returns the result to Drive\n→ Coda/Don picks it up\n```\n\nNothing more needs to be invented around it right now.\n\nSo from here, every decision gets tested against one question:\n\n> **Does this help complete that temporary round trip, or is it black-hole bullshit?**\n\nIf it’s the latter, we cut it.", "text_chars": 662, "code_blocks": 1, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "3eabf79c-ca2d-484d-bf28-c60931ac5ca2", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790366015.357, "updated_at": 1790366034.259782, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "That's it. That's it. Let's cut it. ", "text_chars": 36, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "6c85b301-4a1a-4d08-9abf-b8523bf86d09", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790366019.609114, "updated_at": 1790366019.609114, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "reasoning_recap", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "1f677579-378c-4e9d-ba71-e13e1d8dfc01", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790366019.611748, "updated_at": 1790366033.677333, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Yes. **We cut Cable Car down to the temporary bridge it was supposed to be.**\n\n## Cable Car — stripped scope\n\n**Keep only:**\n\n```text\n1. Drive INBOX\n2. Local GCE inbox/_shared\n3. Local GCE OUTBOX\n4. Drive OUTBOX / returned files\n5. File identity\n6. Hash check\n7. Duplicate protection\n8. Minimal retry/logging\n```\n\nThe operating flow is:\n\n```text\nDrive INBOX\n→ pick up file\n→ local GCE inbox\n→ work happens\n→ local GCE OUTBOX\n→ upload return to Drive OUTBOX\n```\n\n## Cut from the active requirement\n\nWe do **not** need, for this temporary bridge:\n\n- elaborate state-machine enforcement\n- multi-stage lifecycle architecture\n- formal JSON-Schema runtime enforcement\n- giant recovery matrix\n- recurring Coda certification gates\n- numbered slices\n- new governance contracts\n- routing intelligence\n- interpretation\n- scheduling framework beyond a simple poller\n- permanent enterprise-grade transport architecture\n- documentation that pretends this is a platform\n\n`FAILED` and `QUARANTINE` can remain as simple safety buckets if already useful, but they do not get to become another subsystem.\n\n## What survives from the existing build\n\nThe good inbound work stays:\n\n```text\nhashing\natomic copy/rename\nduplicate protection\nreal Drive read\nlocal delivery\nbasic ledger/logging\n```\n\nWe do **not** rebuild inbound just because the previous process got messy.\n\nThe only functional gap that matters now is:\n\n> **Take a file from the existing local outbox and put it back into the designated Google Drive return folder.**\n\nPlus one small operational correction:\n\n> **Make real Drive mode explicit and reproducible so `npm run run` cannot silently use the mock client.**\n\nThat is the job.\n\n### New stop condition\n\nThe project is done for its temporary purpose when Don can demonstrate:\n\n```text\nput document in Drive\n→ document appears locally\n→ put response in local outbox\n→ response appears in Drive\n```\n\n**One round trip. No ceremony.**\n\nAnything that does not contribute directly to that round trip is out of scope.\n\n### Loop check\n\n**CLEAN.**\n\nWe have the knife on it now.", "text_chars": 2062, "code_blocks": 4, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "a164e01e-4317-4ce7-8c9a-f4a6e5a6c195", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790366138.833, "updated_at": 1790366188.614817, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Okay, so I'm gonna tell you what I just told the other chat. We are not going through rounds of certification slices. This is as simple as giving Nico and Space Bunny the tools with subagents. fucking deprecate what we don't need and keep what we fucking need. This better be working in this pass or I'm gonna be fucking pissed today. ", "text_chars": 335, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "ec9d24a3-913f-4f54-b1c0-ecf0f6b505f6", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790366143.319572, "updated_at": 1790366202.395501, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Good. Then the pass needs to be **one coherent demolition-and-finish pass**, not another governance carousel.\n\nSend Nico / Space Bunny this:\n\n:::writing{variant=\"document\" title=\"Cable Car — One-Pass Simplify + Finish Directive\"}\n# GCE CABLE CAR — ONE-PASS SIMPLIFY + FINISH\n\n**AUTHORITY:** Don  \n**SEAT:** Nico  \n**OCCUPANT:** Space Bunny  \n**MODE:** BUILD / SIMPLIFY / COMPLETE  \n**EXECUTION STYLE:** MULTI-SUBAGENT, ONE COHERENT PASS  \n**NO SLICES. NO MID-PASS CERTIFICATION GATES. NO ARCHITECTURE REOPENING UNLESS A HARD BLOCKER MAKES THE ROUND TRIP IMPOSSIBLE.**\n\n## MISSION\n\nTake the current Cable Car project and turn it into the simple temporary bridge Don actually asked for:\n\n```text\nGoogle Drive INBOX\n→ local GCE inbox/_shared\n→ work happens\n→ local GCE OUTBOX\n→ Google Drive OUTBOX\n```\n\nThat is the product.\n\nAnything that does not directly support this temporary round trip should be deprecated, bypassed, removed from the active runtime, or clearly marked non-active.\n\nThe pass is successful only when the round trip works end-to-end.\n\n---\n\n# NON-NEGOTIABLE OPERATING RULES\n\nUse multiple sub-agents.\n\nEach sub-agent gets a bounded lane, but this is still ONE build pass.\n\nDo not stop after each lane for Don/Coda review.\n\nDo not create:\n- Slice 5\n- Slice 6\n- certification packages\n- new architecture documents\n- new contract systems\n- new governance layers\n- new state-machine abstractions\n\nDo not optimize for theoretical permanence.\n\nOptimize for:\n- working\n- visible\n- reproducible\n- simple\n- temporary\n- safe enough\n\n---\n\n# SHARED TODO\n\nMaintain one shared TODO:\n\n```text\n[ ] inspect current repo truth\n[ ] identify keep/deprecate/remove\n[ ] make real Drive mode explicit and reproducible\n[ ] preserve working inbound path\n[ ] implement local outbox → Drive return path\n[ ] ensure duplicate/conflict safety\n[ ] wire simple poll/run command\n[ ] run full round trip\n[ ] fix any defects found\n[ ] rerun full round trip\n[ ] return final outcome\n```\n\nDo not turn TODO items into slices.\n\n---\n\n# SUB-AGENT LANES\n\n## AGENT 1 — CURRENT CODE / KEEP-CUT MAP\n\nInspect actual repo.\n\nClassify every meaningful component:\n\n```text\nKEEP\nDEPRECATE\nREMOVE\nBYPASS\nUNKNOWN\n```\n\nBias toward keeping proven inbound code and cutting unused scaffolding.\n\nExplicitly inspect:\n- contracts/\n- state-machine code\n- recovery code\n- mock client\n- real Drive client\n- config loader\n- CLI\n- tests\n- docs\n- local paths\n\nReturn a practical map, then implement accordingly.\n\n---\n\n## AGENT 2 — INBOUND PRESERVATION\n\nDo not rebuild inbound unless required.\n\nVerify th